\uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HEAT\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning. So, we're talking about his record heat that hit yesterday. Take a look on the East Coast. We saw Delaware, 90 degrees. Syracuse at 88. Even out towards not so Cold Bay, Alaska, 53 degrees.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TODAY'S IMPACTS\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And all of that heat coming ahead of a cold front, so you'll notice things cooling down as head through the days to come. Now that cold front on the leading edge some severe storms. So, two areas to watch from \uc2 Lowe\uc2  Country into Wilmington right on up into the Delmarva Peninsula and the mid-Atlantic. We've got the threat for severe weather. Then you head into the northeast, New England. Heavy rain could lead to flash flooding tonight into Sunday morning. So, keep that in mind.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE THREAT\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The timing on that that moves through this evening, and then we've got a close eye on areas like Texas, where we could see very large hail.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SEVERE THREAT\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're also anticipating to see a few severe thunderstorms roll through as we head into the afternoon. That's a look at the weather across the country, let's see what's going on a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230530ej4m0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 EARTH DAY THE NEXT GENERATION EAGER TO SAVE THE PLANET\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORMS, TRACK\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, BAPTIST, ABORTION PILL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, WAR, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AS CEASE-FIRE FAILS\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, RACISM, TEXTS, BURRIS, THORPE, KHAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SUED IN ALLEGED "RACIST" TEXTS SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, WAR, MILLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE TANKS SENT TO UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 SWAIN, FLOODING, TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEVASTATING RETURN OF TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 AMMUNITION, THEFT, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE AMMO ROUNDS STOLEN\par \par \uc2 METEOR SHOWER, HUMPHRIES, BELGIUM, MILLER HIGH LIFE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 EARTH DAY, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight, on this Earth Day, the next generation eager to save the planet.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Earth Day was first celebrated on this day in 1970. People across the country gathered to raise awareness about environmental issues. From the beginning, students have been front and center. That year, these teenagers leaving their cars at home to ride bikes make instead. A third-grader shows a poster he made about air pollution. And today, the tradition continues. In the Florida Keys this morning, students learning the importance of protecting the world's oceans, releasing two rehabilitated sea turtles.\par \par \uc2 TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 At the top of that yellow flower...\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At this nursery in Tampa, Florida, young students taking a butterfly walk.\par \par \uc2 STUDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We are learning about different types of species of butterflies and we're learning things that butterflies can do.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Outside Chicago, preschoolers put on gloves, picked up shovels and got to work, planting petunias and dropping seeds in the soil, stressing the importance of fruits and vegetables.\par \par \uc2 STUDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It is healthy and we can grow our bodies and get stronger.\par \par \uc2 TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 They can go home and actually tell their parents they want something green or something yellow or red on their plates.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Their experience continuing beyond the garden.\par \par \uc2 STUDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm going to clean up the trash today, so that the Earth can be happy.\par \par \uc2 TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 That's really the bottom line, is the more backyard national parks we create, the better everything is.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A new generation now excited to protect our planet.\par \par \uc2 STUDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Happy Earth Day.\par \par \uc2 STUDENTS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Happy Earth Day.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Happy Earth Day. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230425ej4m0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POLICE SUED IN ALLEGED "RACIST" TEXTS SCANDAL FEDERAL PROBE UNDERWAY INTO CA DEPARTMENT\b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORMS, TRACK\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, BAPTIST, ABORTION PILL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, WAR, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AS CEASE-FIRE FAILS\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, RACISM, TEXTS, BURRIS, THORPE, KHAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SUED IN ALLEGED "RACIST" TEXTS SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the police department in Antioch, California, is under intense scrutiny. Nine officers facing a federal lawsuit over alleged racist texts.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The DA saying, a joint investigation with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  uncovered racist and homophobic text messages between officers.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The police union urging due process for those officers involved. Here's ABC's Jay O'Brien.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL PROBE UNDERWAY INTO CA DEPARTMENT\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the discovery of racist and homophobic and other disturbing text messages allegedly sent between police officers in Antioch, California has now led to a federal lawsuit, accusing officers in the Bay Area city of numerous civil rights violations. The suit based on an investigation by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the Contra Costa County District Attorney's Office, finding between 2019 and 2022 officers texted messages like, "We just ran down a monkey." And, "I sometimes just say people gave me a full confession when they didn't." An Antioch police sergeant allegedly using a racial epithet and writing, "I will bury that blank in my fields."\par \par \uc2 JOHN BURRIS (ATTORNEY FOR PLAINTIFFS)\par \par \uc2 It certainly made me cringe to think that these are the very people who are supposedly serving the people of this community.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One officer allegedly making racist and sexually explicit comments about local activist Shagoofa Khan, now a plaintiff in the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 SHAGOOFA KHAN (COMMUNITY ORGANIZER)\par \par \uc2 It honestly scares me to the point that I want to move out of \uc2 the city of Antioch\uc2  because I feel unsafe here.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Community tensions flaring at a recent city council meeting.\par \par \uc2 MAYOR LAMAR THORPE (ANTIOCH CALIFORNIA)\par \par \uc2 You want to go outside right now (inaudible) ? Apologizing for the racism that is going on in this community. You're the problem.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The investigation identifying 17 police officers who allegedly wrote messages. But the local public defender's office says dozens more may have seen them when they were sent.\par \par \uc2 MAYOR LAMAR THORPE (ANTIOCH CALIFORNIA)\par \par \uc2 This is about a culture. If you're on those text messages and you saw these text messages, and you didn't say anything, that's the problem.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lawyer for the local police union representing some of the officers tells ABC News, "We are hopeful that the investigation will be thorough and objective and will determine culpability where it is deserved." Tonight, the Antioch Police Department not releasing any details about possible disciplinary actions. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jay O'Brien with those new developments, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230425ej4m00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEVASTATING RETURN OF TULARE LAKE CA HOMES AND FARMLAND DESTROYED BY RISING WATERS\b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORMS, TRACK\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, BAPTIST, ABORTION PILL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, WAR, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AS CEASE-FIRE FAILS\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, RACISM, TEXTS, BURRIS, THORPE, KHAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SUED IN ALLEGED "RACIST" TEXTS SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, WAR, MILLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE TANKS SENT TO UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 SWAIN, FLOODING, TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEVASTATING RETURN OF TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meantime, back here at home, the recent heavy rain in California has helped ease the state's drought, but it's also led to the devastating return of Tulare Lake.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Once one of the largest freshwater lakes west of the Mississippi, it had been dry for decades, but is now threatening entire communities in the Central Valley.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Homes, businesses and vital farmland under water. Here's ABC's Kayna Whitworth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CA HOMES AND FARMLAND DESTROYED BY RISING WATERS\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, a frantic race to save communities in California's Central Valley as the Tulare Lake, dried up for decades, has reemerged. You can see the water lapping up here in Tulare Lake for the first time in four decades.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You can see the water lapping up here in Tulare Lake for the first time in four decades. But it's coming onto a road. In fact, this is a Sixth Avenue and it's a main thoroughfare through some of America's most productive farmland. And for the next 10 miles, it's several feet under water.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At least 150,000 acres of farmland and communities are estimated to be flooded after at least 15 atmospheric rivers dumped continuous rain and snow in California this winter. The region, home to the largest dairy-producing county in the nation. Area farmers like Peter DeJong (PH) now scrambling to save their herds.\par \par \uc2 FARMER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 So, it was probably about this height.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, this water...\par \par \uc2 FARMER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, those trees were under.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Many of his crops were drowned.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) $3 to $4 million underwater?\par \par \uc2 FARMER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 USDA\uc2  says agriculture is more than $10-billion industry Tulare and neighboring Kings County. 18% of the country's pistachios are grown here, nearly 16% of our citrus. And in some areas, that water is estimated to be eight to ten feet deep. And as warmer temperatures melt that record winter snowpack in the Sierra Nevada, more water is on the way. Experts say it could be years before the water dissipates.\par \par \uc2 DANIEL SWAIN PHD (CLIMATE SCIENTIST)\par \par \uc2 In the climate change context, we expect to see more severe droughts in California as temperatures rise. We also expect to see more severe floods.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Whit, you can see homes like this. It's been under water for already a couple of weeks. But now, if you look at just this 20-mile stretch of road alone, farmers told me they estimate the economic impact of this flooding to be nearly a billion dollars and more water is on the way. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Striking images. Kayna Whitworth, our thanks to you tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLIMATE CRISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POWER OF WATER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And on this Earth Day, across our ABC News platforms, we have much more on the power of water. Go to the ABC News website or you can scan the QR code right there on your screen.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUG TRAFFICKING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER MARINE SENTENCED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A former active-duty US marine has been sentenced to 144 months in prison for conspiring to import and distribute fentanyl and other illegal drugs into the United States.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Roberto Salazar admitted to recruiting, managing and paying drug couriers. The drugs were concealed in a specially designed car engine compartment. Prosecutors say he also commissioned a Mexican songwriter to write a drug ballad about him.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's much more ahead on "World News Tonight" this Saturday, including that during nighttime rescue.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) How crews located three men trapped in a canyon. And 160,000 rounds of ammunition stolen from police.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230425ej4m00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORMS, TRACK\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, BAPTIST, ABORTION PILL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, WAR, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AS CEASE-FIRE FAILS\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, RACISM, TEXTS, BURRIS, THORPE, KHAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SUED IN ALLEGED "RACIST" TEXTS SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, WAR, MILLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE TANKS SENT TO UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 SWAIN, FLOODING, TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEVASTATING RETURN OF TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 AMMUNITION, THEFT, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE AMMO ROUNDS STOLEN\par \par \uc2 METEOR SHOWER, HUMPHRIES, BELGIUM, MILLER HIGH LIFE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, scientists are trying to determine if a streak of light and a loud boom was caused by a meteor over central Indiana last night.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Doorbell cameras captured the fireball just around 8:00. Local emergency management officials say there were no reports of damage. This comes as the Lyrid meteor shower is reaching its peak across the US.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BARRY HUMPHRIES: 1934 - 2023\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, we note the passing of entertainer Barry Humphries.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He was best known for his stage persona Dame Edna, an over-the-top snob with flamboyant costumes and a razor-sharp wit. It won him a Tony Award in 2000. He was expected to play Dame Edna for a week, but the character lasted for several decades. Barry Humphries died today from complications from hip surgery. He was 89 years old.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And a story that has beer lovers crying foul.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Customs workers in Belgium recently dumped an entire shipment of Miller High Life, and then crossed the cans, more than 2,000 of them. The reason, Miller's slogan written on the cans, the champagne of beers, only use sparkling wine from the Champagne region of France is allowed to use that name. So, the suds did flow but straight down the drain. What a waste.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, a new generation celebrates Earth Day.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230425ej4m00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE SUPREME COURT TOSSES CASE BACK TO APPEALS COURT\b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORMS, TRACK\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, BAPTIST, ABORTION PILL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to our other major headline tonight. The next steps in the abortion pill battle.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Supreme Court letting stand for now access to mifepristone in states where abortion is legal. Two justices, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , dissenting. Mifepristone, which was approved by the FDA more than 20 years ago, is used in the majority of all abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The issue now returns to a lower court. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze from the Supreme Court tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TOSSES CASE BACK TO APPEALS COURT\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, mifepristone remains available to women in states where abortion is legal as the turbulent battle over the abortion pill heads back to an appeals. The Supreme Court late Friday putting a temporary hold on two the global court rulings that, if upheld, would have drastically restricted access to mifepristone, used in more than half of US abortions. Conservative justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and then \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  publicly dissenting.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONSERVATIVE JUSTICES THOMAS AND ALITO DISSENT\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Alito writing, he has legitimate doubts the Biden administration would obey an unfavorable order in the case, indicating he'd let the abortion pill restrictions go into effect.\par \par \uc2 KIMBERLY WEHLE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Alito probably would affirm the Texas court in this case. And remember, Alito was the author of the very controversial Dobbs opinion, which reversed 50 years of precedent protecting women's rights to abortions under the United States Constitution.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCESS TO MIFEPRISTONE INTACT AMID COURT CHALLENGES\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Supreme Court's decision follows a dizzying two weeks that left abortion providers, drugmakers, and millions of women in limbo.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIMELINE: U.S. ACCESS TO MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On April 7th, a federal judge in Texas ruled to suspend FDA approval of mifepristone, which would make it unavailable nationwide. Five days later, the Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals in New Orleans upheld some restrictions, like only allowing the medication to be used up to seven weeks of pregnancy instead of 10. And 24 hours ago, the Supreme Court intervened to delay both of those rulings, kicking off another legal showdown in the appeals court. Tonight, the anti-abortion group behind the Texas lawsuit tells ABC News, it appreciates Alito's dissent and is optimistic about the case.\par \par \uc2 ERIK BAPTIST (SENIOR COUNSEL ALLIANCE DEFENDING FREEDOM)\par \par \uc2 We're going to proceed as we proceeded before successfully in the lower courts and hope that we continue that success in victories at the fifth circuit again.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Abortion rights activists breathing a temporary sigh of relief but vowing a long fight ahead.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCGILL JOHNSON\uc2  (PRESIDENT & CEO PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 We are going to have to continue to, you know, see this play out in the courts while we also continue to fight significant legislation restricting further access to abortion care in many states.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Elizabeth Schulze is joining us now from the Supreme Court. And, Elizabeth, walk us through the next steps in this legal battle.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, oral arguments over the merits of that Texas case are set to kickoff May 17th in the Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals. A ruling is expected to come by the end of the summer. And that could ultimately be appealed back here to the Supreme Court, so the justice would have to decide once again if they will take up this case. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Elizabeth, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230425ej4m00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS SATURDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, breaking news as we come on the air. Multiple severe storms threatening a wide area from the south to the East Coast.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS UNDER SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Twenty-six million Americans are facing a severe weather threat. Central Texas in the crosshairs. Flights disrupted and several airports as dangerous as thunderstorms slammed the I-95 corridor. Sixty-mile-per-hour winds, large hail and tornadoes are all possible as the storms move through. Rob Marciano with the timing and the track.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The battle over the most commonly used abortion pill enters a new phase. The Supreme Court allowing to mifepristone to remain widely available but only for now in states where abortion is legal. What's at stake for both sides as they gear up for the next round in the lower courts? Elizabeth Schulze at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AS CEASE-FIRE FAILS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Evacuations underway in Sudan as a cease-fire fails. Vicious fighting continues. New clashes at an airport. The US military deployment forces in the region, standing by in case they're needed to effectuate embassy staff. Some 16,000 Americans are still in Sudan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SUED IN ALLEGED "RACIST" TEXTS SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A California city and at least nine police officers are being sued over text messages, allegedly racist, homophobic and sexually explicit. The federal lawsuit accusing officers of numerous civil rights violations.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE TANKS SENT TO UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 More times are on their way to Ukraine. Spain sending six Leopard 2 tanks with four more to follow soon. The US now with a major push to train Ukrainian troops on American tanks as Russia bogged down, accidentally bumps one of its own cities.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEVASTATING RETURN OF TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A California lake, dry for decades, now reemerging after record rainfall. The floodwaters threatening to overwhelm communities and crops. The major impact on a vital food supply.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DARING UTAH RESCUE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The daring nighttime rescue. Three college students trapped in a pool of water while exploring canyons. How they called for help miles away from any cell phone service?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HONORING EARTH DAY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And on this Earth Day, the tradition continues and the next generation eager to protect our planet.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight."\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230425ej4m00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 EVACUATIONS AS CEASE-FIRE FAILS SUDAN TO COORDINATE EXITS AS SAUDIS EVACUATE 150+\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORMS, TRACK\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, BAPTIST, ABORTION PILL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, WAR, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AS CEASE-FIRE FAILS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Overseas now and the crisis in Sudan is intensifying. The Sudanese army says it's helping to correlate evacuations of foreigners after a cease-fire failed.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Saudi Arabia and state television airing the arrival of some of its citizens and some from other countries earlier today. Heavy fighting raging in the capital.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) US diplomats at the embassy told to shelter in place. Here's ABC's Ines de la Cuetara.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUDAN TO COORDINATE EXITS AS SAUDIS EVACUATE 150+\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the Sudanese army saying it is coordinating with other countries to evacuate foreign citizens and diplomats despite continued clashes between the two warring military groups, including the main airport. Explosions and gunfire rang out in the streets of the capital, Khartoum. Dark plumes of smoke billowing into the sky. The 72-hour cease-fire announced by both sides on Friday quickly deteriorating. The conflict, which has already claimed at least 400 lives including one American, now entering its second week. Tamir Mohammed's (PH) two children are dual Sudanese-American citizens currently stranded in Khartoum with their aunt, seen here singing with their cousins to distract himself from the fighting.\par \par \uc2 FATHER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We try to contact with the embassy. We sent them many emails. We tried to call. There is no answering sometimes.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Those children among the estimated 16,000 Americans currently inside Sudan, including roughly 70 US embassy personnel currently sheltering in place. US military forces have been deployed to the region, poised to assist with the potential evacuation of the embassy. Some countries already conducting evacuations. Video from Saudi state TV showing dozens of evacuees, including Saudi embassy staff arriving to Saudi Arabia via warship.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And today, the US Embassy in Sudan reiterating to Americans that conditions on the ground currently make it too difficult to undertake a government-led evacuation of private citizens. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thousands of Americans still with an uncertain future there. Ines, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230425ej4m00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINES POLICE AMMO ROUNDS STOLEN/DARING UTAH RESCUE\b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORMS, TRACK\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, BAPTIST, ABORTION PILL, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, WAR, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS AS CEASE-FIRE FAILS\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, RACISM, TEXTS, BURRIS, THORPE, KHAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SUED IN ALLEGED "RACIST" TEXTS SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, WAR, MILLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE TANKS SENT TO UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 SWAIN, FLOODING, TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEVASTATING RETURN OF TULARE LAKE\par \par \uc2 AMMUNITION, THEFT, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE AMMO ROUNDS STOLEN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next tonight, police in Columbus, Ohio, are desperately trying to track down a trove of ammunition that was stolen from a warehouse this month.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) 160,000 rounds were taken. They're used in assault-style rifles and were meant to be delivered to the police training facility. Two people have been arrested in connection with the robbery. The trucks they allegedly used were recovered, but the ammunition has not been found.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DARING UTAH RESCUE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Three college students in Utah say their smart phone got them out of a dangerous situation.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The three were exploring a remote canyon last Saturday when they got stuck in a deep pool of water. They began experiencing hypothermia and had no cell service. But they were eventually able to get help using an iPhone 14, which sends an SOS via satellite. That led to a dramatic nighttime helicopter rescue. The three are now safe and very grateful.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, the mystery fireball caught on camera over the Midwest.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230425ej4m00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON THE SUPREME COURT JUSTICES SET TO ISSUE DECISION ON ABORTION PILL ACCESS BY MIDNIGHT\b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, WIND, HAIL, FLOODING, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 "RUST", BALDWIN, HUTCHINS, CHARGES, GUTIERREZ-REED\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, VIOLENCE, DEATH TOLL, CEASEFIRE, KIRBY, EMBASSY, AHMED\par \par \uc2 SHOOTINGS, ARRESTS, WHITE, WASHINGTON, ROTH\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, MIFEPRISTONE, ABORTION PILL, ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are. Okay, Erielle, thanks very much. Now to the abortion pill battle. The Supreme Court, after delaying a decision on access to the drug, is set to issue a ruling by midnight. Rachel Scott reports from the court. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON THE SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICES SET TO ISSUE DECISION ON ABORTION PILL ACCESS BY MIDNIGHT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning. Well access to the pill used in more than half of abortions in the United States is on the line, with the Supreme Court expected to decide at any moment whether or not new restrictions will go into place on the abortion drug Mifepristone. The Justices blew past their own deadline, giving themselves more time to consider a ruling by a lower court that would only allow the pill to be approved up to seven weeks of pregnancy instead of 10.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Require three in person doctor visits, and no longer allow the pill to be available by mail. Now the Justices do have several options that they can take today, the can allow the restrictions to go into effect, even in states where abortion is legal. They could take up the case themselves nearly one year after Roe V. Wade was overturned by the Supreme Court, or they could send it back down to the lower courts to be worked out.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the high court did give itself until Midnight tonight to make a decision. As for that initial delay, well some experts suggest that on an issue this contentious, there could be multiple opinions in the works, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such a consequential decision. Okay, Rachel, thanks very much. Juju.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230526ej4l00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, breaking news as we come on the air, the Supreme Court decision on the fate of the abortion pill expected at any moment.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DEADLINE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court set to weigh in on the battle over the abortion pill, potentially dealing a massive blow to abortion rights supporters. Mifepristone used in more than half of all abortions in the US. The court's action coming nearly a year after overturning Roe vs. Wade, what this could mean for millions of women across America, even in states where abortion is legal. Rachel Scott standing by.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY BRIDGE FIRE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The deadly bridge inferno shutting down one of the busiest highways in America. A fuel tanker truck rolling over and bursting into flames, the massive fire spreading below the bridge.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORM THREATS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Severe storms sweeping toward the East Coast overnight. Heavy rain and damaging winds moving into the northeast tomorrow. Rob Marciano timing it out.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOOTING SUSPECT SURRENDERS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The neighbor facing charges for allegedly shooting and wounding a 6-year-old girl and her parents when the basketball rolled onto his lawn in North Carolina. The two-day manhunt across state lines, where the suspect finally surrendered.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WEIGHS SUDAN EVACUATION PLANS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Crisis in Sudan. Both sides agreeing to a three-day ceasefire allowing humanitarian aid shipments and citizens to celebrate the end of Ramadan. More than 400 people killed, including an American. The US troops on standby in case the American embassy needs to be evacuated.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER KILLED BY THROWN ROCK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A horrific scene on the highway in Colorado. A young driver killed by a rock thrown through her windshield. Authorities believe it may be linked to five incidents reported within one hour.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCE: BALDWIN GUN FAULTY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Twenty-four hours after prosecutors revealed the decision to drop charges against Alec Baldwin for the deadly shooting on the set of the movie "Rust," a source telling ABC News the gun in his hand was faulty. What they're now saying about how it could have fired even without pulling the trigger as Baldwin has always claimed.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NFL\uc2  PLAYERS SUSPENDED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NFL\uc2  suspending five players, three of them indefinitely, for violating the league's gambling policy including betting on \uc2 NFL\uc2  games.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COCKPIT WINDOW POPS OPEN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the cockpit scare just seconds after takeoff. A United flight making an emergency landing, the pilot's window popping open.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight with David Muir."\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230425ej4l00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEADLINE FOR ABORTION PILL DECISION JUSTICES EXPECTED TO WEIGH IN BEFORE MIDNIGHT TONIGHT\b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, JEAN-PIERRE, WYNN, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. It's great to have you with us on this busy Friday night. I'm Whit Johnson, in for David tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And as we come on the air, access to abortion on this country is on the line.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLINE FOR ABORTION PILL DECISION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) At this hour, the Supreme Court is facing a self-imposed deadline at midnight tonight to weigh in on the abortion pill, used in more than half of all abortions in the US, after a lower-court ruling impose sharp restrictions.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Biden administration has asked the Supreme Court to leave women's access in place. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved the drug mifepristone 20 years ago. If those restriction stand, they would apply even in states where abortion is legal. This comes less than a year after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, ending the constitutional right to an abortion after 50 years.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ABC's Rachel Scott leads us off at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICES EXPECTED TO WEIGH IN BEFORE MIDNIGHT TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, millions of American women watching the High Court and there self-imposed 11:59 deadline to weigh in on the battle of the abortion pill mifepristone after the Biden administration made a direct appeal for the justices to keep the status quo.\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 The President has been very clear, this administration has been very clear, we are going to continue to fight for women's, women's reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At stake, women's access to a pill used in more than half of abortions in the United States. Approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  over 20 years ago, but suspended by a lower court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE SUPREME COURT MIFEPRISTONE ORDERS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Supreme Court expected to decide at any moment. Option one, preserve access to the drug while the case works its way through the courts. Option two, agree with an appeal's court propose restrictions, which will prevent women from accessing the drug after seven weeks of pregnancy, require three in-person doctor visits and make it unavailable by mail. Or option three, agree with the conservative judge in Texas who ruled mifepristone should never have been approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in the first place and should be taken off the market. The court can also decide to take up the case themselves.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This will be the justices' first major decision on abortion nearly one year after Roe vs. Wade was overturned, and it could significantly change the landscape of abortion rights in this country. If restrictions on mifepristone do go into effect, it would impact women in states even where abortion is legal.\par \par \uc2 DANIKA SEVERINO WYNN (VP OF ABORTION ACCESS PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 We should not be in a position where politicians and judges who do not have medical backgrounds are making decisions about medical care.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott joining us outside the Supreme Court. And, Rachel, we're still waiting on that decision tonight. Supreme Court watchers, though, says that this delay could mean there is some disagreement among the justices.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly, Whit. Veteran court watchers suggest that, on an issues this contentious, there could be multiple opinions in the works. Both side of this debate tonight, not only bracing for this decision, but preparing for a very long legal fight ahead. Tonight, all eyes were on the Supreme Court, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll stand by for that important ruling. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230425ej4l00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL BATTLE SUPREME COURT ALLOWS ABORTION PILL TO REMAIN AVAILABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 823 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Special Report\par \uc2 ABSR\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC NEWS SPECIAL REPORT\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT ALLOWS ABORTION PILL TO REMAIN AVAILABLE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. I'm Whit Johnson in New York. And we're coming on the air because the Supreme Court has just issued an important ruling on the abortion pill. The drug mifepristone has been available to women for more than 20 years used in all of half of all abortions in the US. Just moments ago, the Supreme Court preserved full access to the abortion pill for now as the case plays out in the courts, issuing what is called a full stay of that controversial ruling by a Texas judge. Let's get right to ABC's senior Washington reporter Devin Dwyer to break down what this means for us. Devin, what are the judges saying here and what are the next steps?\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, the Supreme Court just released a one-paragraph order in a vote that appears to be 7-2, staying those lower court decisions from last week that would have put severe new restrictions on the most commonly used abortion in America, mifepristone. The Supreme Court said that they are going to put those rulings on hold with two justices dissenting, Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 . They would have granted the denial. They would have allowed those restrictions to take effect. And this effectively means that this case will continue to play out and access to the drug will remain nationwide. Status quo for now. This is a huge relief to the Biden administration and millions of American women and the pharmaceutical industry, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Devin, just to follow up on that. You said that case continues to play out. So, we know we were looking at a few different scenarios. So, does this go back to the lower courts and it's likely and possible that it then ultimately goes back up to the Supreme Court down the road?\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It sure does. And the Supreme Court in that one-paragraph order just now do acknowledge that this could come back to the Supreme Court at a future time. They're going to let the Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals hear the case on the merits. That's already scheduled on an expedited basis for next month. Depending upon how that court decides, that decision can be appealed and it could come back to the Supreme Court at a future date. So, we'll wait to see if the Supreme Court takes it up then. But for now, they're not getting involved and it's status quo.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Devin Dwyer, thank you. Let's bring in ABC's Rachel Scott outside the Supreme Court. Rachel, you've been covering this story for months. I wonder what's expected from both sides after this ruling has come down.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, more legal challenges is exactly what is expected here. While abortion rights advocates are certainly going to be breathing a sigh of relief, they know that this will continue to play out in the courts. And quite frankly, the landscape around abortion rights has already changed significantly since the Supreme Court overturned Roe vs. Wade nearly a year ago. Fourteen states in the country have already stopped nearly all abortion services with many more heading in that direction, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel, thank you. Let's bring our national correspondent Terry Moran on this. And, Terry, what's confusing here is, this is not just about abortion. This is about the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . This is about the power of government agencies. And it could have a widespread impact and possibly involving other medications down the road.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, that was the concern of pharmaceutical companies and investors, no question about it. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  is the gold standard for drug approvals around the world. And this just (inaudible) through chaos into the process. And the industry was very, very concerned. More broadly, on the issue of abortion, when the court overturned Roe vs. Wade, they said, we're going to return it to the democratic process as well. What we see in Texas is that federal judges are willing to take up that battle and advance the effort to ban abortion nationwide.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Terry Moran, our thanks to you. Again, that breaking news coming down from the Supreme Court. Our coverage continues on ABC News Live and abcnews.com. We now return to regular programming. And for many of you, that's "World News Tonight." For now, I'm Whit Johnson in New York. Good night.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 This has been a special report from ABC News.\par \par \uc2 Document ABSR000020230425ej4l00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA'S AGING WATER INFRASTRUCTURE DISTURBING LOOK AT THE TAP WATER IN ONE LA TOWN\b0\par\par\uc2 1,339 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 HADID, SOBRIETY, SUPERMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\par \par \uc2 FINANCES, HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS, ADVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTING FOR HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET THE MOST OUT OF YOUR MONEY\par \par \uc2 BLUE, SWIMSUIT, CHILDREN, SAFETY, SCARNATI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\par \par \uc2 KITCHENWARE, PLANTS, LAUNDRY, BEDDING\par \par \uc2 MANATEE, HABITAT, RESTORATION, CRYSTAL RIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANATEE MIRACLE IN CRYSTAL RIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW A COMMUNITY CAME TOGETHER TO RESTORE HABITAT\par \par \uc2 TAP WATER, SAFETY, TASTE, HEALTH, COBURN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAP WATER TASTE TEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO IMPROVE THE QUALITY OF WATER IN YOUR HOME\par \par \uc2 WATER, INFRASTRUCTURE, SAFETY, ENVIRONMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICA'S AGING WATER INFRASTRUCTURE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DISTURBING LOOK AT THE TAP WATER IN ONE LA TOWN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to continue with that theme now and look at the tap water in one Louisiana town, what it means for the aging water infrastructure in hundreds of other places across America. Senior national correspondent Steve Osunsami has the story. Good morning, Steve.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, George. It's something we take for granted. One study shows that of the 2.2 million miles of waterline that run from water plants like this one into American homes, that more than half of them need fixing.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There are times when a name fits a little too well, and that's how it feels in rural Louisiana in this very real town called Waterproof, where even the mayor said most things here have seen better days.\par \par \uc2 MAYOR JARROD BOTTLEY (WATERPROOF LOUISIANA)\par \par \uc2 It's becoming a norm for me to get up in the morning and twist the knob and no water.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The irony is they're surrounded by water. The mighty Mississippi runs right behind the levies that keep the town dry. But what happened here in 2018 now happens all the time. A waterline broke down, and they had to go months without life's most necessity flowing into their homes.\par \par \uc2 WATERPROOF RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It's broke anywhere, fix it.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH CAMERON (WATERPROOF RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 We've been on, doing this for three weeks, and we're going into another month.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Even when it's working, sometimes this is what comes out of the tap.\par \par \uc2 MAYOR JARROD BOTTLEY (WATERPROOF LOUISIANA)\par \par \uc2 So at that point, we get bottled water to warm in the microwave and put on a towel to take a bath.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow. That's how you take a bath, warm it in the microwave, put it on a towel.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Marcella Rollins, who runs a food truck, says that the water lines here will freeze and break whenever it gets cold.\par \par \uc2 MARCELLA ROLLINS (WATERPROOF RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Well, I know when it got snowy in March, and we didn't have any water for two months, we had to go get a motel. I had some friends bring me 30-gallon trash cans full of water from Vidalia so that I can wash clothes.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The problems in Waterproof are old waterlines that they've bandaged too many times, and it's an American problem. Some of the oldest waterlines in the country were laid down in the 1800s, before Henry Ford built his first car and before women won the right to vote. And they should have been replaced 100 years ago.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACING A WATER CRISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOUISIANA'S INFRASTRUCTURE RANKS AMONG THE WORST IN AMERICA\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Louisiana is one of 10 states that get near failing grades for their water system. Families here have \uc2 Facebook\uc2  pages where they share videos of brown water.\par \par \uc2 WATERPROOF RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 So, this is the new showerhead on the left. This is the old one after a year. Look at that. That's so gross.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How far back do the water mains go?\par \par \uc2 MAYOR JARROD BOTTLEY (WATERPROOF LOUISIANA)\par \par \uc2 Oh, gosh, 1964. We should have changed meters and updated lines six times by now. So, the hot, I'm now in the hot seat.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One look downtown shows why that seat is so warm, the fewer and fewer people to pay water bills.\par \par \uc2 MAYOR JARROD BOTTLEY (WATERPROOF LOUISIANA)\par \par \uc2 This is Main Street, the humor in that, huh?\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They're now getting $10 million in help from the state and federal government to update the parish water plant and build a new reservoir so if the pumps fail, like they sometimes do, they can still send water shooting down the line. But it won't be enough to fix this leaking water tower or replace any of the underground water mains that parallel the decline of the town. Marcella Rollins says she'll\u160\'00\'A0gladly pay a little more for her water if it would mean a little less suffering.\par \par \uc2 MARCELLA ROLLINS (WATERPROOF RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 I love to feed people.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They remind us here that clean running water means life and health and should never stop flowing.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Experts say that the real solution for towns like Waterproof and, frankly, every city in America, is something that many people won't like to hear, which is to raise the cost of water. They point out that, you know, we'll gladly spend a dollar for a bottle of water at a grocery store or $7 or $8 for that same bottle in a hotel but then get mad at water bills that are higher than $50 a month. And guys, they that say if you want to see where the next Waterproof is going to be, look for any community that promises to keep monthly water rates low. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Steve, thanks very much. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And big thanks to Ginger and our great crew out on the Crystal River. What a (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Incredible day. Also, check out two big NHL playoff games tonight on \uc2 ESPN\uc2 . The biscuit drops on the Lightning's and Maple Leaf's at 7:00 Eastern, and you've got the Kraken facing the reigning champ, The Avalanche, at 9:30.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Thanks so much for watching. Have a great day.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 780 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2 