CHILDREN, SAFETY, SCARNATI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\par \par \uc2 KITCHENWARE, PLANTS, LAUNDRY, BEDDING\par \par \uc2 MANATEE, HABITAT, RESTORATION, CRYSTAL RIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANATEE MIRACLE IN CRYSTAL RIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW A COMMUNITY CAME TOGETHER TO RESTORE HABITAT\par \par \uc2 TAP WATER, SAFETY, TASTE, HEALTH, COBURN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAP WATER TASTE TEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO IMPROVE THE QUALITY OF WATER IN YOUR HOME\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, let's go to Ginger in crystal river, Florida. Hey, Ging.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLLEN FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, we're just watching the grazing manatee around us, but you remember all that record heat we were talking about just last week? Well, that also meant record pollen. Yes, this is segment is sponsored by... It's that time of the week when are here in Crystal River. We did, a couple weeks ago, see all this pollen over the water, but it was nothing like what was happening in Maryland. Look at all that green and white pollen building up around boats. That's Kent Narrows, Maryland. Wow. The high pollen levels still sticking around this week, the mid-Atlantic, as well. Do you see that map? The pinks and the reds are coming in. You know it's bad when that goes down. So, all you need is to burst out a few more of those trees. But so far this morning, my allergies are all right, right down here. So we'll keep it that way. And for now, that's the big picture. Let's get a check a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Eva is back now with an interview that I bet you only heard wah, wah, wah, wah, just looking, right?\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He was as wonderful as you could imagine that he would be. Coming up on "GMA3," Gio and I sat down with Aquaman himself, Jason Mamoa, about why he was meant for that role and his off-screen work to help protect our water.\par \par \uc2 JASON MAMOA (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. Aloha, I'm Jason Mamoa, and I am super-stoked to be part of this Earth Day special, "The Power of Water." Okay, so tune in to "GMA3" to see how I'm making waves to save our planet, (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) On "GMA3's" "The Power of Water" show airs today at 1:00 pm, guys. He's doing so much, and he still feels like he's not doing enough.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you have your wedding ring on.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) it was a Zoom interview. Of course my husband noticed right away.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Eva, thank you. Coming up why getting a glass of water from your tap is impossible for some depending on where you live.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "GMA's" pollen report is sponsored by...\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 IPHONE WARNING THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\b0\par\par\uc2 783 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, we are back now with a warning for iPhone users about how criminals are stealing phones and locking people out of their accounts forever.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It is a story we first saw in the "Wall Street Journal." And Whit Johnson has more on how to keep your information safe. So important. Good morning, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It sure is. Rebecca, good morning to you. So, thieves are turning the tables on this one and using an iPhone security setting against their owners, denying them access, sometimes permanently.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Forty-six-year-old Greg Frasca says his iPhone was stolen in October 2022 and he's still blocked out of his account. He says he's tried just about everything, even offering \uc2 Apple\uc2  a DNA swab and $10,000 to a charity of the company's choice. No luck.\par \par \uc2 GREG FRASCA (VICTIM OF IPHONE THEFT)\par \par \uc2 The biggest struggle has been, you know, getting back those photos and videos that I keep of my daughter, my family, birthdays, anniversaries.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "The Wall Street Journal" reporting thieves are now exploiting an iPhone security setting called the recovery key, a unique 28-digit code meant to protect you from online hackers. But instead, they're using it against their victims.\par \par \uc2 JOANNA STERN (SENIOR PERSONAL TECH COLUMNIST "THE WALL STREET JOURNAL")\par \par \uc2 The thieves make the code. And the owners of the phone don't actually have the code. So, they can't get back into their accounts.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Once a thief has access to your phone's passcode, they can easily go in, change your \uc2 Apple\uc2  ID password and enable the recovery key themselves.\par \par \uc2 JOANNA STERN (SENIOR PERSONAL TECH COLUMNIST "THE WALL STREET JOURNAL")\par \par \uc2 They call \uc2 Apple\uc2 . And \uc2 Apple\uc2  says, sorry, we need that recovery key to get you back into your account.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, you're locked out. And without that key, it's almost impossible to regain control of your account, making sensitive features like \uc2 Apple\uc2  Pay and financial apps incredibly vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 DR RICHARD FORNO (ASSISTANT DIRECTOR UMBC CENTER FOR CYBERSECURITY)\par \par \uc2 Once your phone is unlocked, you have essentially unlocked probably the keys to your personal kingdom. Once that happens, anything could happen.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: APPLE STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Apple\uc2  saying in a statement, "We sympathize with people who have had this experience and we take all attacks on our users very seriously no matter how rare. We work tirelessly every day to protect our users' accounts and data and are always investigating additional protections against emerging threats like this one."\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Experts say there are things that you can do to protect yourself, including setting a complicated passcode, making a separate screen time password through parental controls.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WAYS TO PROTECT YOURSELF\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Make sure to use a fingerprint reader or face ID when you're using your device in a crowded space. And consider storing your photos and videos through another cloud service like \uc2 Google\uc2  Photos or \uc2 Dropbox\uc2 , so even if your phone gets stolen, you won't lose those precious memories, guys.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is great information, Whit, especially the idea of storing your photos elsewhere, really smart.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The important things, right?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks, Whit. "Play of the Day" is next.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FATAL GARAGE COLLAPSE INVESTIGATION NEARLY 100-YEAR-OLD BUILDING HAD SEVERAL OPEN VIOLATIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the investigation into the deadly parking garage collapse in New York City.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FATAL GARAGE COLLAPSE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEARLY 100-YEAR-OLD BUILDING HAD SEVERAL OPEN VIOLATIONS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We're learning the building had several open violation. And there's new video showing the moment of collapse. Trevor Ault is on the scene. Good morning, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. So, this morning, officials are still telling people in six buildings surrounding this parking garage that they have to stay away because the structure is still unstable. And as that's going on, we're learning more about the victims of this collapse and history of the building leading up to it.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, new video inside that New York City parking garage capturing the moment it collapsed.\par \par \uc2 ANGELA TRAVLOS (NEIGHBOR)\par \par \uc2 My whole apartment shook like an earthquake.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Every floor pancaking to the ground, cars tossed into a pile of rubble, injuring seven people and killing the building manager, who neighbors say was trying to leave for the day when the structure caved in. Demolition workers seen here methodically removing each car one by one, trying to avoid further collapse of the unstable structure.\par \par \uc2 ZACH ISCOL (EMERGENCY MANAGEMENT COMMISSIONER)\par \par \uc2 Right now, we're transitioning to how we safely take down that building. And it's incredibly complex.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Manhattan district attorney says his office will investigate the cause. Sources say they're focused on the weight from those 50 cars on the roof, and also noting the building's age constructed in 1925.\par \par \uc2 EXPERT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 And a building that's 100 years old, you're going to have these defects.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2003 VIOLATIONS\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to the Department of Buildings records, the garage has several open violation, including one deemed hazardous from 2003, citing defective concrete exposed with rear cracks. The mayor's office though, confirmed the garage owners did make repairs to that problem in 2010, and was not cited in future inspections, but they neglected to file the correct paperwork to close out the citation. Still the sudden collapse raises concerns about aging structures particularly those with visibly cracked concrete.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we have reached out to the owner of this parking garage now multiple times, but we have yet to hear back. And this morning, we're hearing already the heavy machinery from these demolition crews as they're slowly taking it apart, taking down the rest of the structure. And their goal, they say, is to make sure they don't do any damage to the surrounding buildings. Linsey?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We can, of course, understand why that's so important. Trevor, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,005 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 HADID, SOBRIETY, SUPERMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\par \par \uc2 FINANCES, HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS, ADVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTING FOR HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET THE MOST OUT OF YOUR MONEY\par \par \uc2 BLUE, SWIMSUIT, CHILDREN, SAFETY, SCARNATI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to a GMA parenting alert. A swim instructor on TikTok is urging parents not to buy a certain color bathing suit for their children. Eva Pilgrim is back with why. Hey, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, it's probably something parents probably have never factored in, the color of your child's bathing suit. We went to the pool to see how different colors make it easier or harder to spot when your kid is struggling in the water.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI SCARNATI (MOM & SWIM INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 This is why you do not put your children in blue bathing suits.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a clothing choice that could save your child's life.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI SCARNATI (MOM & SWIM INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 Look how difficult it is to see her under the water.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Swim instructor and mother of two Nikki Scarnati going viral after posting this video on TikTok, urging parents not to dress their kids in blue bathing suits, saying it's difficult to see children in water when they are wearing blue or even white.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI SCARNATI (MOM & SWIM INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 And I think for many parents, seeing is believing. Even look in the sunlight. Look how difficult it is to see her with that bathing suit on because it's the same color as our environment. Neon orange, neon yellow, neon pink, those three would be the best way to go. If neons are not available, then I would recommend red, orange, bright pink or yellow. And this is in calm water. This is not with a whole bunch of other kids playing and splashing around and having a good time.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to the CDC, drowning is the leading cause of death for children ages one to four. The National Drowning Prevention Alliance says avoiding blue suits could help prevent drownings. We took to the water with a chief aquatics officer Brendan O'Melveny of Imagine Swimming and his two young daughters to see the blue suits in action for ourselves.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you can really see with that color on how hard it is to see her in the water.\par \par \uc2 BRENDAN O'MELVENY (IMAGINE SWIMMING)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, especially when it's a little wavy, and she starts moving around. Yeah, it can be difficult.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When she just went in I was like, where is she?\par \par \uc2 BRENDAN O'MELVENY (IMAGINE SWIMMING)\par \par \uc2 Ready? One, two, three, under. You can see that the bright colors make her a lot more easy to spot.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, you can see that orange is really bright. But water safety is about more than just clothes. Experts say teaching your kids to follow basic poolside rules can make all the difference.\par \par \uc2 BRENDAN O'MELVENY (IMAGINE SWIMMING)\par \par \uc2 It can be just teaching them to wait to get into the water until a parent or other responsible adult invites them in and lets them know that it's safe, learning what lifeguards are, how to recognize them and things like that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HER METHOD TO KEEP KIDS SAFE IN THE POOL\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what else can you do to keep your kids safe? Well, the National Drowning Prevention Alliance recommends five layers of protection. One, barriers and alarms, supervision, water competency, that's learning how to swim for children, but also for adults, life jackets and emergency preparation. Have a phone nearby always when you're by the water so you can call 911. And learn how to perform CPR. Guys, I was shocked how quickly the children disappeared in the water in the blue swimsuits.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Happens so fast.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'd never even considered. Only fluorescent bathing suits from now on.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, definitely. Important information. I think about it a lot with my four-year-old. I'm definitely going out to buy the fluorescent suits. Thank you, Eva.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Eva, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS EARTH DAY SPECIAL\b0\par\par\uc2 1,463 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 HADID, SOBRIETY, SUPERMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\par \par \uc2 FINANCES, HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS, ADVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTING FOR HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET THE MOST OUT OF YOUR MONEY\par \par \uc2 BLUE, SWIMSUIT, CHILDREN, SAFETY, SCARNATI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\par \par \uc2 KITCHENWARE, PLANTS, LAUNDRY, BEDDING\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is a good morning because it is time now for "Deals & Steals." And Tory is back with day two of our Earth Day special. All of the products this morning are from small businesses. Go right to the deals by pointing your cell phone camera at that QR code on the screen. Great to see you, Tory, good morning.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm excited for us to do this together.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm so excited. You came, you came in your Earth Day dress, preparation.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Prepared, yes. I got the memo. I got the memo.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you've got the great stuff here. So, let's start with this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: W&P DRINKWARE\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're starting with w&p. And what's great about this, they're really on a mission to help us eliminate or minimize our reliance on single-use plastic. So, one of their signature products right here is the porter glass. We've got to to-go mug, which feels really good in your hand. It's a nice silicone outside and then a spill-resistant lid, as well. We also have their insulated tumblers, which are great. I quite frankly love their little ice cube trays to make that little teeny, cubed ice.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those are cute.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We even have their cocktail or mocktail kits, depending on your choice. Everybody is slashed at least in half, starts at $20. It's a good one.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Excellent deal. Also, I like that this has some heft to it, so you can really hold it.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It feels really nice in your hand.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEE'S WRAP FOOD STORAGE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, up next, eco-friendly food storage.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, this is Bee's Wrap, and what's great about this is just with the warmth of your hand, you're able to wrap either some bread, a sandwich, a piece of fruit. You can even use this as a bowl cover instead of using plastic wrap or aluminum wrap. This really does replace those single-uses. And what's great is you can wash and reuse it over and over again. So, you get a lot of mileage out of these.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it stays closed.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It stays closed, absolutely it will stay closed, and they wash nicely. They're all made in America, which is kind of another benefit of these. And then when they're done, they're compostable. But you'll get a lot of use out of them. These single and sets start at $7.50.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Excellent.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GREENPAN COOKWARE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, a "GMA" favorite.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is a favorite. This is GreenPan. These, we've got two different stainless sets from them. What's great that they're known for is all of their very healthy non-cook, non-, their coating.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nonstick.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Their nonstick coating. Yeah, thank you, their nonstick coating because it requires a lot less oil, allows you to have much healthier cooking. And then on this one in particular for the stainless, it's got a special exterior that's going to allow it to stay gleaming just like this indefinitely. So, it's not going to discolor, which sometimes happens because of the heat, doesn't happen with GreenPan. We've got two different sets, a three-piece frypan set and 17-piece cookware set. All slashed in half, starts at $90.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good for the earth and less scrubbing. We love that.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, okay.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MODERN SPROUT PLANTS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Grow your own food with these kits.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Modern Sprout, these are really fun. These are all about no green thumb and teeny spaces. So, what I love is that they're style forward and space friendly. We've got lots of options from them. This one, you could do a candle, and then you can grow something in the vessel after. We've got rosemary here, mint here. We even have in the front, they make these really cute terra cotta ones. So those aren't, you're not going to eat, but you can grow a bonsai, a cactus, aloe at home. These are great for anybody, and they're really fun for families to do together. Slashed in half, they start at $9.60.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I can see kids really enjoying that project.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FRIENDSHEEP DRYER BALLS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, shorten drying time, save money.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, Friendsheep. You can cut your drying time with these dryer balls, they happen to be really cute, too, by 20 to 40 percent, which is really amazing. They're also more affordable than single-use, disposable drying sheets, 100 percent wool, absolutely no plastic in them. They look really cute, and they'll last about 1,000 loads, which, for depending on how much laundry you do, is two to four years. These sets are terrific. They start at $9.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love the lady bug.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're so fun.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHEETS & GIGGLES BEDDING\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, here we have our bedding.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, we have our bedding. So, this is Sheets & Giggles, and we've got literally everything, from their natural cooling eucalyptus mattress, this is beloved for full spine support, it's very great support. We've got their pillows. We have their bedding. These are super-soft blankets that we have from them. And what I like is that it's a eucalyptus (inaudible) fabric, so it's sustainably made. It's cooler than cotton. It feels really good. It's temperature regulating, so you're going to be cool in the summer and then cozy in the winter. We've got everything for you to choose from online. It's all slashed in half, from $50 to a little over $1,000, and free shipping.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We love how you got us covered every single day. Tory Johnson, thanks so much. And remember, we've partnered with these companies on these great deals. You can get them on our website, goodmorningamerica.com. And coming up, Ginger is in Florida where a community came together to save its manatees.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSIS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MIDAIR MELTDOWN PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to a Southwest passenger's outburst over a crying baby that forced the plane to land before its destination. Eva Pilgrim is here with the story. Good morning, Eva. I can't imagine what that was like for both the parents and the passengers.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This, the video is insane, y'all. This man lost it. He was on a Southwest flight with a screaming baby. And let's be real, we all know that stinks. But what he chose to do got him kicked off that plane.\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Stop yelling.\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 So is the baby.\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Okay, so, you're a man.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, it's a midair meltdown of epic proportions aboard one Southwest flight. Not just from the baby on board, but also from an adult passenger.\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Lower the baby's voice.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This passenger seen losing his cool after a baby was crying for an extended period of time. Flight attendants pleading with him to stop yelling.\par \par \uc2 FLIGHT ATTENDANT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Let's be rational for a second. There is nothing we can do about this child.\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 No. Let's not, no, no, no.\par \par \uc2 MONIQUE PASS (PASSENGER)\par \par \uc2 All of a sudden, this guy just started screaming at the top of his lungs. It was simply a good five minutes or so. And it was just getting worse and worse and worse.\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you want me to scream? Do you want me to scream? I'll (censored by network) scream. Please stop the baby.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Fort Lauderdale-bound flight landing in Orlando and all the passengers forced to deplane. As for that adult passenger...\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I got rights.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOUTHWEST AIRLINES STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26he was met by security at the gate. Southwest releasing a statement saying, "We commend our crew for exhibiting outstanding professionalism while handling a challenging situation and we appreciate the patience of our other customers on board that had to experience the behavior."\par \par \uc2 JOHN NANCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think the number one thing to say here is that, even though the crews handle things as diplomatically as they can, at the end result, if you don't sit down and close your mouth and stop doing whatever it was you were doing, you're going to be hauled off by police at the other end.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I can tell you as the parent of a small child, I know you guys all have children as well, no one wants their child to scream ever, let alone on a plane with a bunch of strangers. But sometimes it's just unavoidable. My pro tip, and my husband has tested this out repeatedly, noise-canceling head phones. They do work.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They do work. That's right.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For all the...\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So necessary. All right, Eva, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the abortion pill battle. The Supreme Court delayed its decision on access to the drug, which is now expected by tomorrow. Our senior national correspondent Terry Moran is at the Supreme Court with more. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Linsey. As of this morning, access to the abortion pill for women in America remains the same as it has been for years. But all that may well change by midnight tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The justices decided to give themselves a little more time, extend their own deadline to consider a sweeping ruling by that federal judge in Texas, which would sharply restrict access to the abortion pill. The restrictions that that judge ordered would require that the pill be approved only for the first seven weeks of pregnancy instead of the current ten, also requires three in-person doctor's visits as opposed to the one doctor's appointment today, which can be done by telehealth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIFEPRISTONE RESTRICTIONS\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And it would also no longer allow the pill to be available by mail. Now, the justices have several options here. They could allow those restrictions to go into effect. And that would immediately change access to the abortion pill across America or they could block those restrictions while the case is litigated or they could take the case up themselves and once again decide a major case on women's access to abortion care in this country just one year after they overturned Roe vs. Wade.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we will know, as I say, by midnight tomorrow. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot of focus on that deadline. All right, Terry Moran, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to Florida, where the Board of Education expanded the don't say gay bill. Senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott is here with the latest on that. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning. It's been dubbed don't say gay, a law in Florida that restricts what teachers can tell their students about sexual orientation and gender identity. Up until now, this only applied to children from kindergarten through third grade, but Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ' is pushing to expand it to include all students through high school. The Florida Board of Education approved the restrictions, which states, "For grades four through 12 instruction on sexual orientation or gender identity is prohibited unless such instruction is either expressly (inaudible) by state academic standards or if it is part of a reproductive health course or health lesson for which a student's parent has the option to have his or her student not attend." A spokesperson for DeSantis has signaled that he supports this move. It's expected to go into effect in the coming weeks. But critics warn this policy is dangerous and says students who may be struggling will now be cut off from the teachers who could help, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Rachel Scott, thanks so much for being with us here in studio today.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 722 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America, it's 8:00 am.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Overnight, deadly tornados in the heartland leave a trail of destruction. Oklahoma slammed, massive hailstones rain down, smashing this windshield, this assisted living facility destroyed. We're live on the scene this morning, and Ginger is tracking where the severe weather is heading next.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS AND ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The new study about kids and ADHD drugs and potential misuse. What parents need to know.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL BELLA HADID\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Bella Hadid's sobriety journey, the supermodel celebrating six months without drinking. What she's saying about her relationship with alcohol.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATHING SUIT WARNING\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 "GMA" parenting alert, why a swim instructor and mom of two is urging parents not to buy their kids blue bathing suits and the basic water safety rules everyone should know as this swim season heats up.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAP WATER TASTE TEST\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tapping into the water in your home, how you can find out if what's coming out of the faucet is safe and what you can do to make it taste better. Becky Worley is on the case.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANATEE MIRACLE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Manatee miracle in Crystal River, how a Florida community came together after the storm of the century 30 years ago to rescue and restore the habitat of these lovable animals.\par \par \uc2 FLORIDA RESIDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Look at her go, look at her go.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And wait until you see the manatee snack bar. Ginger is there live, and you may even see some in the water this morning. It's all ahead as we say good morning America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning America. Hope your Thursday is off to a good start. Let's go down to Ginger in Crystal River with the manatees. Hey, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hey, we are just flanked by manatees, so we're trying to make sure we can get them on our underwater cameras so that you can see. But, do you see the smile plastered on my face? How often do I get to smile when I'm telling an environmental story? But this one deserves a smile and more. Thirty years ago, this whole ecosystem was wrecked by the storm of the century. It took away all the manatee food. But boy, the populations have come back. It is a beautiful story how it just is a testament to what people can do in helping the environment. And how is this going to apply to other places where manatee aren't doing as well? You'll find all that out coming up.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we see you, Ginger. We also saw those manatees swimming around her. We could almost see their smiles. Also ahead, a lot of people are moving their money to high-yield savings accounts, so we're going to break down what they are, how you can make the most of your money. That's all ahead.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 HADID, SOBRIETY, SUPERMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\par \par \uc2 FINANCES, HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS, ADVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTING FOR HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET THE MOST OUT OF YOUR MONEY\par \par \uc2 BLUE, SWIMSUIT, CHILDREN, SAFETY, SCARNATI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now let's go back to Ginger in Crystal River, Florida.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Linsey. We are just seeing manatee everywhere, from our drone, we've got an underwater camera. We're bringing you the latest on that in a moment.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we do have to talk about the severe weather. You saw Mireya earlier, talking about the deadly tornadoes in Oklahoma. There were 15 reported tornadoes, and there are also really big hail, some hail there from Hartford and Middleton, Wisconsin, the pictures and the video of it kind of rushing down the street with all the flooding. But you also have the potential for violent storms again today. It's really going to start after 2:00, 3:00 pm, so Dallas, it's early afternoon for you, a move there later in the afternoon and evening for San Antonio all the way up to St. Louis. This is a damaging wind threat, but there are isolated tornadoes, and of course you could see big hail because some of the tops of these storms could get, you know, 50,000 feet high, so really big.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Then it's going to keep marching east, and we will eventually be seeing the Southeast pick up on this. Saturday, the damaging wind threat extends for much of Eastern North Carolina down to coastal South Carolina and Georgia, so Savannah, Charleston all included. And we get the heavy rain, that's Saturday night into Sunday, but if you're in Washington, DC, and you've got afternoon plans, keep an eye on the thunderstorms that'll be blowing through after you see 90 degrees tomorrow. That's the big picture. Let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION ONGOING\b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Staying in New York now, mayhem in Midtown when a car plowed right through an outdoor restaurant. Andrew Dymburt has that story. Good morning to you, Andrew.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And good morning, Lindsey. It was a wild seen here in New York. The video is hard to watch.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It all started when the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  attempted to pull over a black Cadillac for potentially driving with a fake license plate. The driver speeding through the Manhattan streets trying to evade officers before plowing right through an outdoor dining structure, nearly missing a female pedestrian. The driver also taking out a street sign and fire hydrant before escaping on foot. By the way, that pedestrian that was nearly hit was missed by inches if you take a look at the video there. Now, during the chase, though, an officer was struck, sustaining an injury to the head. He was rushed to the hospital, but is expected to survive. Meanwhile, no arrests in this case have been made just yet and the investigation is still on going.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But really, harrowing video there. Hard to watch, especially with all the pedestrians that were out there and dining outdoors in the middle of busy Midtown in the middle of the day. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank goodness no one was hurt. All right, Andrew, thanks so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MANATEE MIRACLE IN CRYSTAL RIVER HOW A COMMUNITY CAME TOGETHER TO RESTORE HABITAT\b0\par\par\uc2 1,596 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 HADID, SOBRIETY, SUPERMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\par \par \uc2 FINANCES, HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS, ADVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTING FOR HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET THE MOST OUT OF YOUR MONEY\par \par \uc2 BLUE, SWIMSUIT, CHILDREN, SAFETY, SCARNATI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\par \par \uc2 KITCHENWARE, PLANTS, LAUNDRY, BEDDING\par \par \uc2 MANATEE, HABITAT, RESTORATION, CRYSTAL RIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANATEE MIRACLE IN CRYSTAL RIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW A COMMUNITY CAME TOGETHER TO RESTORE HABITAT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now for our series, "The Power of Water," and this morning, Ginger is in Crystal River, Florida, with a real success story for the manatees that make the river their home. Hey, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, it is not often I get to tell you a climate or environment story with a happy ending or a solution that's happening now. But this one has all of it. So yes, it's not about the power of water, it's about the power of people, the agency we have in changing and helping the environment around us, the waterways and how they cleared them here for the water, yes, but also the adorable inhabitants, the manatee.\par \par \uc2 FLORIDA RESIDENT (CHILD)\par \par \uc2 Oh, there's two.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a magical moment, getting a glimpse of Florida's gentle giants, the manatee. They congregate here every winter in Crystal River, which boasts bathtub-clear water just off Florida's west coast.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Crystal River is fed by more than 70 freshwater springs that I'm in right now. They stay 72 degrees year round. That's warmer than the ocean in the winter months, so they become a critical winter habitat for more than 800 manatee.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) On March 12, 1993, this critical ecosystem was wiped out by a devastating storm dubbed the storm of the century.\par \par \uc2 LISA MOORE (SAVE CRYSTAL RIVER)\par \par \uc2 It virtually killed all the vegetation. It was a lot of saltwater that came in here, and the freshwater vegetation couldn't take it.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It has taken decades, fueled by community advocates and more than $40 million in funding from the state and private donations. The river has been restored to pristine conditions after removing 400 million tons of debris and other detrimental material and stabilizing the shore lines to protect from future monster storms, not to mention planting a lot of manatee food.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How much is a manatee eating on a daily basis?\par \par \uc2 RYAN BRUSHWOOD (SEA & SHORELINE)\par \par \uc2 I believe the statistic is that a manatee can eat about 10 percent of its bodyweight a day. So, you've got to think, if it weighs 1,200 pounds, that's 120 pounds of grass. They have quite the appetite.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) To satisfy that appetite, more than 450,000 clusters of eel grass have been planted underwater by hand, creating more than 300 acres of manatee food. I got to help plant the last batch.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When sea grass or eel grass goes in, you plant it, but then it spreads?\par \par \uc2 RYAN BRUSHWOOD (SEA & SHORELINE)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. So, the grass here specifically can spread seven feet in any direction in one year. They sequester nutrients, nitrogen, phosphorus, carbon, and they\u160\'00\'A0can completely transform a water body that provides benefits to not only the ecosystem but to the community through ecotourism and just healthier, cleaner water.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While Crystal River is a shining example of a habitat restoration, manatees elsewhere are threatened by speeding boats and, along Florida's east coast, in the Indian River Lagoon, starvation. Excessive pollution from development, leaking septic systems and agricultural runoff have all caused massive algal bloom, killing off the sea grass manatees that rely on. In 2021, a record-breaking 1,100 manatee deaths were reported statewide and another 800 in 2022. While the number of manatee deaths has decreased this year, experts say they're still at high risk.\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTEER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Ready? One, two, three.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Groups like Zoo Tampa rescuing and rehabilitating more than 300 of these lovable creatures. I got to join in and release two of them.\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTEER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Look at her go. Look at her go.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Would you consider this release a success?\par \par \uc2 TIFFANY BURNS (ZOOTAMPA)\par \par \uc2 A hundred percent. Their story isn't over. We will continue to watch to ensure that these animals continue to stay safe, and they continue to do the things they need to to thrive.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The newly released manatees will enjoy what the team likes to call manatee munchies at the manatee snack bar, daily feedings until they're ready to survive on their own. Sea and Shoreline, the company that restored the manatee habitat here, is now turning to the Indian River Lagoon, an even more ambitious undertaking, aiming to replicate the success they had at Crystal River.\par \par \uc2 TIFFANY BURNS (ZOOTAMPA)\par \par \uc2 Once you fix it, you don't want to let it go backwards. You have to make people care by showing them what it could be and what can you do to help.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right off the front of the boat, we have a manatee mom nursing a manatee baby. It is the sweetest thing to see. But helping and being out here and being part of the solution, it really, like, takes over your entire body and soul because you want to make the glory of these waters and these animals have everything they could. There are a lot of ways to do that. I know that we learned some in the piece, but George, it's inspiring, that's for sure.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Boy, it sure is. That water is just crystal clear. So, has there been a difference in the behavior of the manatees since the river's been cleaned up?\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know what? There have been a difference in the behavior of all the animals. Come on in. This is Paul Cross, director of operations of Plantation at Crystal River. I know the crews we've been with said that you're seeing other fish, you're seeing other birds that haven't been here in decades coming back because it's so clean. But have you seen the manatee act differently? And then also, what can we do to help to make sure when we come down here to see them, that we're good to them?\par \par \uc2 PAUL CROSS (PLANTATION ON CRYSTAL RIVER)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, the manatees are phenomenal here, right. So, normally they come to thermoregulate. Now what we're seeing is they're staying longer and feeding. They're constantly feeding, as you've seen this morning, you know, you see the crumbles coming off of them, you know. But the word to the public, I would say, is the key is to slow the boats down, right? Manatees like to hang out in five to seven foot of water. That's where we like to boat. You know, so pay attention to your signs, slow the boats down whenever you can.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because that's really how they get hurt, and then, of course, the fertilizer. As we just learned in the piece, you know, fertilizer is one thing that we all have agency over, and that is what creates algae that then takes over their food source. So, we're going to keep looking for mom and baby out here, guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Ginger. Boy, that was really something, wasn't it?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It was great. Coming up, Becky Worley is back with a tap water taste test, how to know if your water is safe.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HUNTING FOR HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS HOW TO GET THE MOST OUT OF YOUR MONEY\b0\par\par\uc2 984 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 HADID, SOBRIETY, SUPERMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\par \par \uc2 FINANCES, HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS, ADVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTING FOR HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET THE MOST OUT OF YOUR MONEY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn to your money now. With high interest rates, many people are withdrawing their money out of traditional bank accounts, putting them into high-yield savings accounts. Rebecca, walk everyone through this.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so what we've seen in the last year is that interest rates have been going up, and that means you pay more money to take out a loan, a mortgage, a car loan, but where you get paid more is on your bank account. At the same time, not all banks are created equal, not all accounts are created equal. So if you just left your money in your traditional savings account, on average that APOI would have been 3.9 percent over the last year. A high-yield savings account interest rate is more like four-plus percent. However, like I said, you've got to go looking for it, and there are some smarter ways to do that than others.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO LOOK FOR IN A HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS ACCOUNT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME BANKS OFFERING INTEREST RATES OF MORE THAN 4%\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, for people who maybe have a tax refund, they want to put it in a high yield savings account, what should you be on the lookout for?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW IS IT DIFFERENT FROM A TRADITIONAL SAVINGS ACCOUNT?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, the number one thing is that it's an \uc2 FDIC\uc2 -insured account. That's really important because that means if that bank goes out of business, you are guaranteed to get your money back by the \uc2 FDIC\uc2  up to $250,000. You also want to look for things like no minimum deposit and balance requirements, no monthly fees. And then you also want to make sure that if you're going to do that, that they do have a competitive interest rate, and that should be four-plus percent. You also can look at CDs if you want to stay inside your bank. CDs are often offering similar rates. The thing is, your money will be tied up then. You won't access it for the time of the CD.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Are you skeptical at all, I'm sorry, George, are you skeptical at all about the online bank versus, like, the brick-and-mortar, traditional banks?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's important to remember you get a different service with the online bank. Your money, if it's \uc2 FDIC\uc2  insured, still as safe as any other type of bank. But you're not going to necessarily have that high-touch experience. There's no brick-and-mortar bank that you can walk into and say, I have a question. Oftentimes, they don't have phone numbers that you're going to be calling regularly. Most of your interactions are going to be over email, over the internet. You have to be comfortable with that.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What are the other pitfalls?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO KNOW & WHAT TO LOOK OUT FOR\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, there are some big issues with the confusion that can exist in the banking system in general. And the most important thing to really keep in mind is that you're looking for these \uc2 FDIC\uc2 -insured accounts. We've heard a lot about crypto. People got really excited about crypto. That is not necessarily a place, that's definitely not a place that's \uc2 FDIC\uc2 -insured, so you have to be careful about that. And then you want to check for withdrawal limits and fees and then remember that that interest rate is subject to change over time.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, if you have a little extra change, it's a good time.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It does not hurt to look, and the people who have looked have really made a lot more because of compound interest. That means interest on your interest that's in the account.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, good to know. Thank you, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 07:30 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA." There's Ginger on the beautiful Crystal River in Florida. She's with the Sunshine State's gentle giants, talking about the manatees. Their precious ecosystem was almost completely wiped out, but the community came together to save them. That's all coming up. A real story about hu-manatee there.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Whoa, nicely done.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Been working on that all morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're following a lot of headlines as well, including the deadly outbreak of tornadoes overnight across three states.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Eight tornadoes touched down just in Oklahoma killing at least two people.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "RUST" RESUMES PRODUCTION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, the production of Alec Baldwin's movie "Rust" resumes today for the first time since the deadly shooting of cinematographer Halyna Hutchins in October of 2021. Filming is now taking place on a movie ranch in Montana. Baldwin faces charges of involuntary manslaughter in New Mexico. He has pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEWLY-DECLASSIFIED UFO VIDEOS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, right now, the Department of Defense is investigating 650 encounters of mysterious objects in the sky, 140 more than last year. But the director of the Pentagon's new office reviewing UFO incidents told lawmakers they found no credible evidence of alien activity or evidence that Russia or China is behind it. But there are concerns about the advancing technology in those countries.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW COVID BOOSTER RECOMMENDATIONS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the CDC is now recommending a second dose of the latest COVID booster for people 65 years and older and those with compromised immune systems. The booster is designed to target the Omicron variant. Eligible people can get it four months after their last dose.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA WHAT'S NEXT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we've got a lot more ahead, including that warning for iPhone users. Thieves have a new way of stealing your device, even locking you out forever. That's all coming up. George?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER 