 SAFETY, SCARNATI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\par \par \uc2 KITCHENWARE, PLANTS, LAUNDRY, BEDDING\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to GMA, live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 HADID, SOBRIETY, SUPERMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's a beautiful day in our neighborhood, and we are back now with our, on "GMA" with our cover story. Supermodel Bella Hadid is celebrating six months of sobriety and getting candid about her relationship with alcohol. And Stephanie Ramos has more. Good morning, Stephanie.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey there, good morning, Rebecca. Bella Hadid has joined the ranks of celebrities ditching alcohol, revealing that she is celebrating a sobriety milestone. And her fans are loving it.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From the runway to the red carpet to rocking dozens of magazine covers, Bella Hadid is having a moment. And this morning, the 26-year-old supermodel says she is celebrating a new milestone, six months alcohol-free, posting this screen grab Tuesday to her \uc2 Instagram\uc2  of an app that tracks sobriety in real time. Hadid sharing her journey on social media last month, posting this TikTok video that's racked up more than 6.4 million views, with the caption, "Five months alcohol free." Fans quick to comment, one writing, "Yes, let's normalize not drinking alcohol, please," another writing, "Bella Hadid is sober, so I became sober."\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This isn't the first time Hadid has opened up about her relationship with alcohol. Last January, in an interview with "InStyle," saying, quote, "I have done my fair share of drinking. I loved alcohol, and it got to the point where even I started to, you know, cancel nights out that I felt like I wouldn't be able to control myself."\par \par \uc2 KRISTINA WANDZILAK-GIORGI (ADDICTION SPECIALIST)\par \par \uc2 It used to be that you had to be an alcoholic to take a break or to get sober, you know, and it's not the case today. And I love seeing this whole younger generation, like, doing it different and trying different things and learning how to connect with each other without using a drug.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hadid joining other stars like Chrissy Teigen, Drew Barrymore and Cheryl Burke, who have all been open about their own road to sobriety.\par \par \uc2 KRISTINA WANDZILAK-GIORGI (ADDICTION SPECIALIST)\par \par \uc2 Actually, it can create some accountability and a lot of support if you have millions of followers that are joining you and celebrating you along the way. It actually provides a lot of encouragement.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Bella was recently named to "Time" magazine's 100 most influential people list for 2023. And we are seeing the influence she has on young people and letting them know that it's okay to not drink alcohol. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Stephanie.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\b0\par\par\uc2 621 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to \uc2 Facebook\uc2 's class action settlement and how to know if you qualify. Becky Worley is here with the details. It's so nice to have you with us in studio. Becky, good morning.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, it's great to be with you guys. Rebecca, good morning. If you used \uc2 Facebook\uc2  any time between 2007 and 2022, you could have money coming to you, but you have to register. So, quick rewind.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Back in 2018, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  was all over the news for the Cambridge Analytica scandal. Remember the personality quiz that exposed your user data without your permission even if you didn't take the quiz? Well, \uc2 Meta\uc2 , \uc2 Facebook\uc2 's parent company, denied wrongdoing but settled for $725 million in a class-action lawsuit. That settlement is just now open for distribution. \uc2 Meta\uc2  telling ABC News, "We pursued a settlement as it's in the best interest of our community and shareholders." Adding, "Over the last three years, we revamped our approach to privacy. We look forward to continuing to build services people love and trust with privacy at the forefront," Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, that handled some of it. But for people who want to do this, you have to register. How do you do that and how much money are we talking about, Becky?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. Well, one of those questions is unanswerable. So, let's go to the ones that we can answer. To register, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  will notify users about the settlement using the notifications icon at the top of your \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page if you qualify. Or you can check out a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  user privacy settlement website where you enter your \uc2 Facebook\uc2  information and how you'd like to receive payment. As for the amount, that is not knowable right now. The math goes something like this. $725 million minus legal fees divided by all the people who register, which could be millions, maybe tens of millions of people. I became a journalist because I was told there'd be no math. And I do not want to do the math on this one.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I love, math, Becky. I think it's going to be $0.37. I'm only kidding. But unfortunately, after the legal fees, it tends to be not that much, but good for people to go out and register because showing that you care about this and the outcome important as a consumer.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Privacy first.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Becky, thanks so much. And we know you're going to be back with us for some water test tasting.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Oh, yeah, I'm all over the map today.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Safety, safety and flavor, I see.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I'm here.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks, Becky.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN? WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to allegations that the investigation into \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is being mishandled. Chief justice correspondent Pierre Thomas joins us with more from Capitol Hill. Good morning, Pierre.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rebecca, good morning. We've been waiting for months to see whether the investigation of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  will result in charges. But now, allegations that the President's son has been getting preferential treatment.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, ABC News learning that an \uc2 IRS\uc2  whistleblower is challenging assurances by the Justice Department that the investigation into \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is not being watered down.\par \par \uc2 MERRICK GARLAND\uc2  (US ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 The US attorney in Delaware has been advised that he has full authority. He has been advised that he is not to be denied anything that he needs. He's not restricted in his investigation in any way.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But in a letter to Congress obtained by ABC News, an attorney representing an IRS agent who claims to be involved in the case says his client knows of details of preferential treatment and politics improperly impacting decisions in the investigation.\par \par \uc2 MARK LYTLE (ATTORNEY FOR IRS WHISTLEBLOWER / PARTNER NIXON PEARBODY)\par \par \uc2 He's lost sleep over whether to come forward. And, you know, at the end of the day, he's decided that he would feel worse about himself if he did nothing and stayed quiet.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The attorney for the agent whose name is being withheld until he gets whistleblower status is not named the target of the probe. But sources telling ABC News, he's talking about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . The President's son, who says his name will be cleared, has been under investigation by the Justice Department since during the Trump administration. One part of the investigation involving his taxes. Another involving whether he made a false statement on a gun purchasing form. Sources told ABC News that last fall, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and ATF concluded there is enough evidence to bring charges on both fronts.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTOPHER WRAY\uc2  (DIRECTOR FEDERAL BUREAU OF INVESTIGATION)\par \par \uc2 There is an ongoing investigation run by US attorney out of Delaware from the prior administration. Our Baltimore field office is working very hard with that US attorney, and I expect them to pursue that case.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But after all these months, no resolution from a Trump-appointed US attorney that the Biden administration and attorney general have allowed to remain in place to avoid the appearance of meddling.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But despite those assurances, the Hunter Biden case will now likely get even more scrutiny. The Republican chairman of the House Oversight committee is demanding answers and is accusing the Biden administration of blocking efforts to bring tax charges against \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Pierre, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TAP WATER TASTE TEST HOW TO IMPROVE THE QUALITY OF WATER IN YOUR HOME\b0\par\par\uc2 1,172 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 HADID, SOBRIETY, SUPERMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BELLA HADID'S SOBRIETY JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMODEL CELEBRATES SIX MONTHS ALCOHOL FREE\par \par \uc2 FINANCES, HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS, ADVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTING FOR HIGH-YIELD SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET THE MOST OUT OF YOUR MONEY\par \par \uc2 BLUE, SWIMSUIT, CHILDREN, SAFETY, SCARNATI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIM INSTRUCTOR MOM'S WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY SHE SAYS TO STAY AWAY FROM BLUE SWIMSUITS\par \par \uc2 KITCHENWARE, PLANTS, LAUNDRY, BEDDING\par \par \uc2 MANATEE, HABITAT, RESTORATION, CRYSTAL RIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANATEE MIRACLE IN CRYSTAL RIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW A COMMUNITY CAME TOGETHER TO RESTORE HABITAT\par \par \uc2 TAP WATER, SAFETY, TASTE, HEALTH, COBURN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAP WATER TASTE TEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO IMPROVE THE QUALITY OF WATER IN YOUR HOME\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now on GMA with our series, "This Greenhouse," and Becky Worley is back, and she's talking tap water, from how to tell if the water in your home is safe to how to improve the taste. Hey, Becky.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning again. The water we drink is fundamental to our health, but there is some scary stuff in the headlines about water that's been tainted. So, how can you check the quality of the drinking water from your tap, and what are the options if you want to purify it?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Jordan and Stuart Coburn from El Paso, Texas, this simple act presents a dilemma.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN COBURN (EL PASO RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 The water tastes like metal to me, and then after you drink it, there's an aftertaste. And so I just feel like there's no way to drink it.\par \par \uc2 STUART COBURN (EL PASO RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Got a cup. I almost gagged. I was like, "What is this?" I know we've tried a small Brita filter before, but it's just, it's like two glasses, and then you'd have to fill up the thing again.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Which leaves them using bottled water as a backup.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN COBURN (EL PASO RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 It seems cheap at the time, but then with how much water you're going through, it ends up being a lot more expensive. And then, I hate all the waste that it creates.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Which begs the first question, is this water even safe to drink?\par \par \uc2 DR. SHANE WALKER (UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO)\par \par \uc2 We have both natural contributions of some chemicals in water either from the rocks, the minerals the water flows through, or there can be, sadly, human-caused contamination of the water that could be from industry. It can result in undesirable taste and odor.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN COBURN (EL PASO RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 I've looked up on some websites to see what could possibly be in our water, and there are some that have a lot of scary names on them, a lot of\u160\'00\'A0scary chemicals.\par \par \uc2 STUART COBURN (EL PASO RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 My mind just wanders, and I'm like, "How old are these pipes?"\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) To try to find out, we start by doing what everyone in the country who's on municipal water can do, look up the water report online, which will list everything in your tap water. We asked Dr. Shane Walker to look at El Paso's water report.\par \par \uc2 DR. SHANE WALKER (UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO)\par \par \uc2 Look at each category of chemicals and look at the range of that chemical, and I noticed that they were all well below the maximum contaminant levels, MCLs, so that's really good. The water is meeting the Safe Drinking Water Act requirements.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And does this match what the Coburn's water is comprised of? Well, we do\u160\'00\'A0an independent test, and...\par \par \uc2 DR. SHANE WALKER (UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO)\par \par \uc2 The analysis performed on that sample showed very similar results, very consistent with the consumer report that El Paso Water provides the residents.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO CHECK IF IT'S SAFE & IMPROVE THE TASTE\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But that still leaves the taste issue, but filters can help. Whole house filtration, they can cost $300 to $2,000. Under-sink systems for your kitchen, they're discreet, and they average 250 bucks, and countertop systems, they really run the gamut, from $100 to more than $1,100. But the Coburns realized all they needed to do was up the size of their pitcher.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN COBURN (EL PASO RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Our Brita is working wonders, I feel. I don't taste anything bad anymore. The water tastes great.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If you want to check on the water in your area, you're in luck. Every community water provider in the US is mandated by the \uc2 EPA\uc2  to publish their water report. You can find it online. And finally, one more idea for filtering your water. This is a tap purifier. You just unscrew the little nozzle that goes on your tap, and then you put this up here, no tools needed. You just screw that thing in. You want to shop for something that says NSF, which is National Sanitation Foundation. That's an independent organization that tests and certifies these kind of water purifiers. But this is 35 bucks, easy to install, and your water will hopefully taste a little better.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Becky, great tips. And that, for $35, you got it solved.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, that's, like, cheaper than a Brita.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PLAY OF THE DAY\b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Fresh off a commercial break photo op, Gio is back with "Play of the Day."\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that's right, George. Listen, they call themselves the skydivers over 60, 101 of them gathered in California.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And after the fourth attempt, they got that snowflake formation. Now, they tried to do this last year, but bad weather kept them from perfecting the formation. Well, listen, if we say it's never too late to try, then it's never too late to try again. And this time they got it. The previous record was set back in 2018 with 75 sky divers over the age of 60. Pretty good. Now, the records from this event was 101 people will be submitted to the Guinness World Records.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, how exciting, huh? Imagine doing that at 60.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If I jump out of a plane, something has gone terribly wrong. You guys have ever done it?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, no, no, no. And, in fact, I think "GMA" was trying to get me to do it and I kept them at bay.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was shocked. Oh, Simon just said it's okay.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sixty is not that old.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, that's correct. That's right.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Usually (inaudible) to 85. I don't want to do it at 40. I'd much rather do it much, much later.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thanks, Gio. Coming up, Tory Johnson is celebrating Earth Day with green "Deals and Steals" for your home. It will also save you some green, too.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SHOT TEEN'S REMARKABLE RECOVERY NEW PHOTO SHOWS RALPH ON THE MEND AS SUSPECT APPEARS IN COURT\b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to get the latest now on Ralph Yarl, the Kansas City teen who was shot after ringing the wrong doorbell.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOT TEEN'S REMARKABLE RECOVERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW PHOTO SHOWS RALPH ON THE MEND A SUSPECT APPEARS IN COURT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The family has released a new photo showing the teen on the mend as the man who shot him appeared in court. Alex Perez is in Kansas City with the latest. Good morning, Alex.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. This was Andrew Lester's first appearance in court since the shooting a week ago today. Now, 84-year-old Lester enter a not guilty plea. He's charged with felony assault and armed criminal action.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lester, prosecutors say, twice shot 16-year-old Ralph Yarl after the teen mistakenly rang the doorbell at Lester's home thinking it was a different house. Now, Yarl, who was picking up his two younger siblings suffered life-threatening injuries, authorities say. He had emergency surgery to remove bullet fragments from his skull, but his recovery has been remarkable. After that critical treatment, he was well enough to be released from the hospital Saturday. And this morning, our first look at Yarl at home. This picture shared by the family attorney. The teenager outdoors sitting on a bench, smiling. His family says he is talking and they believe it is a miracle that he is alive.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, that homeowner is due back in court June 1st. If convicted, he could face life in prison. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Alex, thanks so much. Over to you, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And turning now to the \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  rocket set to take off after a failed first attempt. Our transportation correspondent Gio Benitez is here with the latest. Good morning, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Linsey, good morning to you. Yeah, they're going to try again. And if it works, it will become the most powerful rocket on Earth.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  scrubbed the launch on Monday for Starship because of a pressurization issue. And now, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  hopes to launch it later this morning, sending Starship into Earth's orbit. Now, this is a critical test so that someday it can launch humans to the moon and back, maybe even Mars. Starship has seen its fair share of explosions before. And Musk says, if even one of its engines fails, the whole thing may explode.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, Musk has been trying to lower expectations on this, giving it a 50/50 chance of failure. So, guys, if you ask me if this is going to launch, I'll say, eh.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's not so convincing, Gio.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But he did get his 420 potential launch. Congratulations, Elon.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, he did. There you go. I was skipping over that, but you mentioned it.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:43, IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up, the new way thieves are stealing iPhones. What to know about the recovery key and how to protect your information.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But first, we head back to Ginger who's on the Crystal River in Florida for us this morning. Hi, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey there, Rebecca. We are hypervigilant watching for the footprint, that telltale sign that there are manatee.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And boy, let me take you to the drone because we have seen several already this morning. We are bringing you the manatee that are healthy and happy living. And actually a mating pod that we've already come across this morning in the Crystal River because they have put a lot of effort into rehabilitating the water here. The power of water and community, plus groups like Sea and Shoreline that have turned this whole place around. On top of all that, I do have to tell you that Washington, DC could see their first 90-degree temperature tomorrow of the season.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR WARM UP\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that's ahead of those storms, of course, that are going to come through. The warm up does blossom across much of the mid-Atlantic and the northeast before we get all that rain. Let's get your local weather now in 30 seconds. And more manatee coming, too.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also, coming up, guys, I'm the mom of a 4-year-old. This story really struck me. A swim instructor and mom of two has an urgent warning ahead this summer. One color swimsuit you should not buy for your kids. It's a really important one. And we'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "GMA." Let's go ahead and start with a video because the snow is melting and, boy, is that starting the flooding concerns. And the flooding concerns will only broaden as we get into next week. The video you see there is Stillwater, Minnesota. Stillwater where you've got you know, the bridge is almost up, you know, the water is up to there. What I want to show you is this is not the only region and it's not the only day that we'll be talking about this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSISSIPPI RIVER FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's going to broaden as that water keeps filling into the Mississippi River. That northern basin of the Mississippi is where we're going to be watching for flood stages that could approach the highest in more than 20 years. Now, I just heard a (makes noise), and that is a tell-tale sign we are surrounded by the wonder of the manatee here in Crystal River, Florida.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Thirty years ago, this whole ecosystem, all of the food for the manatee was wrecked by what was known as the storm of the century.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, the community really came together with groups like Sea and Shoreline, and they have rehabilitated this water. The power of water and the power of people to help and how it will apply to other places where manatee aren't doing well. Your local news\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 KIDS & ADHD DRUGS NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 EDUCATION, GENDER IDENTITY, SEXUAL ORIENTATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA EXPANDS SO-CALLED "DONT SAY GAY" RULES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIMITS APPLIED TO ALL SCHOOL GRADES\par \par \uc2 ADHD, MEDICATION, MISUSE, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS & ADHD DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY: ONE IN FOUR STUDENTS MISUSING MEDS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to a new study about ADHD medication misuse in students, and Erielle Reshef is back with that. Hi, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good to see you again, Rebecca. It's a wakeup call for parents and school administrators. That study, which was collecting data over 15 years, found one in four students were misusing ADHD medication. It's a problem that's widely known on college campuses, but this is the first national study to look at misuse among middle- and high-schoolers. The study also found schools with a high rate of treatment for ADHD had a 36 percent increased chance of those drugs being misused, suggesting that children with legitimate prescriptions may be sharing it with their friends.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The study identified a correlation of misuse of medication in schools with more white, college-educated parents and with moderate or high rates of binge drinking. Stimulant medications are needed by kids with ADHD, but they can lead to health risks when misused, including cardiovascular conditions, depression, overdoses and psychosis. Experts are urging parents to talk to their children about the risks of giving their stimulant medication to others or taking medication not prescribed by your doctor. Guys.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really disconcerting stuff there. Erielle, thank you. Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," supermodel Bella Hadid is pulling back the curtain on her sobriety journey.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also this morning, how to make the most of your money. More people are turning to high-yield savings accounts over traditional banks. We'll tell you about it.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, as we count down to Earth Day, Becky Worley is here with a tap water test, how to know if it's safe to drink and improve thee taste. And Toy Johnson has\u160\'00\'A0ecofriendly "Deals & Steals" for your home, all ahead, coming up ahead right here on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, ALITO, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS DECISION ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTENDS PAUSE ON LIMITS TO ACCESS UNTIL TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, LYTLE, WRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT FOR HUNTER BIDEN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: WHISTLEBLOWER CLAIMS MISHANDLING OF PROBE INTO PRESENT'S SON\par \par \uc2 PARKING GARAGE, COLLAPSE, SAFETY, TRAVLOS, ISCOL\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER PLOWS THROUGH OUTDOOR DINING RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2  OFFICER HIT BY VEHICLE; INVESTIGATION INTO INCIDENT ONGOING\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, \uc2 FACEBOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 'S $725 CLASS-ACTION PAYOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU MAY QUALIFY TO RECEIVE A PIECE OF THE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE FOR THE WARRIORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN STATE DOWN TWO GAMES IN FIRST ROUND PLAYOFF SERIES\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, RECOVERY, LESTER\par \par \uc2 WHITE, SINGLETARY, ROTH, MONAHAN, GILLIS, TONNER, GUNS\par \par \uc2 BEHAVIOR, PASSENGER, SOUTHWEST AIRLINES, BABY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER LOSES COOL OVER CRYING BABY\par \par \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 , STARSHIP, LAUNCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO LIFTOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND ATTEMPT TO LAUNCH WORLD'S LARGEST ROCKET\par \par \uc2 IPHONE, THEFT, FRASCA, STERN, FORNO, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IPHONE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: THIEVES ARE EXPLOITING A SECURITY SETTING TO LOCK OUT USERS\par \par \uc2 SKYDIVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, SOUTH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 15 TWISTERS CARVE PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But first, we do begin with a deadly twister in the heartland killing two people. Mireya Villareal is on the scene in one of the hardest hit areas, Shawnee, Oklahoma. Good morning again Mireya.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Linsey. Right behind me you can see the amount of debris that is here. This kind of stuff is scattered all over Shawnee. If you take a look over to my left, though, you can see the destruction has hit really the business area of this town, downed power lines everywhere, and take a look up above. That CVS sign, metal, completely knocked down by the powerful winds.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight a deadly outbreak of twisters across three states, leaving a trail of destruction, eight reported tornados touching down just in Oklahoma, \uc2 Accuweather\uc2  capturing this one moving through the town of Cole. In McClain County, at least two people dead, multiple reports of injuries and people trapped in shelters, Shawnee, Oklahoma, getting hit hard.\par \par \uc2 TORNADO SURVIVOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 This is the \uc2 Lowe\uc2 's hardware store, and it looks like some of the roof took damage from the storm.\par \par \uc2 TORNADO SURVIVOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 That's so sad.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Heavy winds damaging buildings, toppling trees, downing power lines and\u160\'00\'A0wrecking cars.\par \par \uc2 TORNADO SURVIVOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 My car is literally not where I left it. All the windows are shattered.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This twig turned into a flying missile, punching a hole through the steel of this car door while this assisted living facility destroyed, leaving dozens without shelter.\par \par \uc2 TORNADO SURVIVOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 The girls had started getting people in their bathrooms and then pulling people away from the windows. So, they're the heroes tonight.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There is no power in this area, but we have continued to drive very carefully through these neighborhoods to make sure we assess the damage. Families are breathing a sigh of relief. They say that while there is damage to their neighborhoods, this could have been way worse. And we do know that power crews are already making their way into these neighborhoods, into these cities, to try and start bringing up that power later this afternoon. George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Big job ahead. Okay, Mireya, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230525ej4k0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL BATTLE BEFORE SUPREME COURT DECISION EXPECTED ON PILL'S AVAILABILITY DURING APPEAL\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 DOMINION, FOX NEWS, SETTLEMENT, NELSON, BROOK, POULOS\par \par \uc2 COLLAPSE, GARAGE, INJURED, VIOLATIONS\par \par \uc2 LEAK, DOCUMENTS, ARREST, TEIXEIRA, COURT\par \par \uc2 STARVATION, SUDAN, FOOD, AID, CLIMATE, CHAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "EVERYBODY LOVES RAYMOND"\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, LESTER, BOND, MERRITT, SPOONMORE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, MIFEPRISTONE, \uc2 FDA\uc2 , APPEAL\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it's good that he's recovering at home. And his mother is a nurse and other family members are medical professionals, and that certainly does help. Alex, thank you so much. Now to the battle over the abortion pill. The Supreme Court is expected to issue a ruling that could have a broad impact on the drug's availability. Our senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott is in Washington with more. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE BEFORE SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DECISION EXPECTED ON PILL'S AVAILABILITY DURING APPEAL\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning to you. All eyes are on the Supreme Court this morning, which could decide at any moment whether women will face new restrictions on the abortion drug Mifepristone. This is a drug that was approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  more than 20 years ago, it's used in more than half of abortions in the United States. Today the Supreme Court will decide whether to take up the case at all.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If it does, whether to allow Mifepristone to stay available as it considers it, or whether to allow new limitations to go into place. Those restrictions would only allow the abortion pill to be available up to seven weeks of pregnancy instead of 10. It would require three in person doctor visits in order to obtain the drug.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And would no longer make it available by mail. Since the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade nearly a year ago. 14 states have stopped nearly all abortion services. But if these new restrictions do go into place, this would apply to every single state in the nation, including the 36 states where abortion is still legal. Robin.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAMAR HAMLIN CLEARED TO PLAY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rachel, thank you. Coming up next, \uc2 Buffalo Bills\uc2  player Damar Hamlin now cleared to play football. Two of the doctors who helped save his life join us next live here only on "GMA." We'll see you then.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230524ej4j0005t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE CHILDREN OF THE WATERS THE STRENGTH OF THE CHILDREN\b0\par\par\uc2 179 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GILLIS, ROTH, RODRIGUEZ, MONAHAN\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, LESTER, YARL, MERRITT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOMEOWNER PLEADS NOT GUILTY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, CALIFF, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT DELAYS ABORTION PILL DECISION\par \par \uc2 GARAGE, COLLAPSE, TRAVLOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY PARKING GARAGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 SOUTH SUDAN, CLIMATE CHANGE, NALL, CHAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE CHILDREN OF THE WATER\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEAKED SECRET INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 SOUTH SUDAN, CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A final note before we go tonight after our trip to South Sudan.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The lasting image for us, the strength of the children. The smiles right there. The fist bump from the little girl in the dress, and then all of the children wanting in. The waves, the smiles, and really everywhere we went, the resilience.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Again, if you would like to help, you can go to wfpusa.org/abcsouthsudan. And we've shown this to you before. Sometimes all it takes is one of these nutritional packets. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230420ej4j00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 134 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GILLIS, ROTH, RODRIGUEZ, MONAHAN\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, LESTER, YARL, MERRITT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOMEOWNER PLEADS NOT GUILTY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, CALIFF, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT DELAYS ABORTION PILL DECISION\par \par \uc2 GARAGE, COLLAPSE, TRAVLOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY PARKING GARAGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 SOUTH SUDAN, CLIMATE CHANGE, NALL, CHAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE CHILDREN OF THE WATER\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEAKED SECRET INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, we are tracking severe storms across the Midwest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORMS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tornado watches in effect across six states. Texas to Iowa, large hail, damaging winds, possible tornadoes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIN FORECAST\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Heavy rain into the northeast by week's end as well.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When they come, the image we cannot forget.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230420ej4j00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINE LEAKED SECRET INVESTIGATION\b0\par\par\uc2 146 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GILLIS, ROTH, RODRIGUEZ, MONAHAN\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, LESTER, YARL, MERRITT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOMEOWNER PLEADS NOT GUILTY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, CALIFF, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT DELAYS ABORTION PILL DECISION\par \par \uc2 GARAGE, COLLAPSE, TRAVLOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY PARKING GARAGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 SOUTH SUDAN, CLIMATE CHANGE, NALL, CHAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE CHILDREN OF THE WATER\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEAKED SECRET INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the Massachusetts air national guardsman accused of leaking highly classified Pentagon documents in court in Boston today.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A lawyer for Jack Teixeira asking the judge for more time to prepare for his detention hearing. And prosecutors may reveal new details about the investigation when they return to court in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back here, tornado watches across several states right now, and those storms then move east.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230420ej4j00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 COURT DELAYS ABORTION PILL DECISION JUSTICE ALITO SETS NEW FRIDAY DEADLINE\b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GILLIS, ROTH, RODRIGUEZ, MONAHAN\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, LESTER, YARL, MERRITT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOMEOWNER PLEADS NOT GUILTY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, CALIFF, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT DELAYS ABORTION PILL DECISION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the breaking news late today for the Supreme Court on the abortion pill. Women's access to the abortion pill remains unchanged in this country for at least two more days. But, of course, the question is, what happens after that? ABC's Rachel Scott at the Supreme Court tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE ALITO SETS NEW FRIDAY DEADLINE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, that urgent ruling from the Supreme Court allowing the abortion pill mifepristone to remain widely available for at least two more days. The justices giving themselves until Friday night to consider a ruling by a lower court that would slap restrictions on the pill to prevent women from accessing the drug after seven weeks of pregnancy, require three in person doctor visits and make it unavailable by mail.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIFEPRISTONE TO REMAIN WIDELY AVAILABLE FOR NOW\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It comes after a conservative Texas judge ruled that mifepristone, which is used in more than half of abortions in the US, should have never been approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . Today, the agency's commissioner said the decision could have ripple effects on other drugs.\par \par \uc2 HONORABLE DR \uc2 ROBERT CALIFF\uc2  (COMMISSIONER \uc2 FDA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 We are concerned about the potential future impacts of this case.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott live at the Supreme Court tonight. And, Rachel, the justices obviously allowing this drug to remain widely available at least until Friday, that's just a couple of days here, giving them more time to reach a decision. Of course, always the question, was there any indication of what direction they are heading in here?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, David, many veteran court watchers suggest that on an issue this contentious, there could be more multiple opinions in the works, which the justices need more time to write. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, live at the court tonight. Thank you, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230420ej4j00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, several breaking stories, a chilling series of shootings across several states in the US after mistakes. This time, two cheerleaders shot after getting into the wrong car at a grocery store. We also have breaking news from the Supreme Court on the abortion pill and what this means. And the severe storms, the tornado watches up across several states as we come on tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILLING SERIES OF SHOOTINGS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 First, tonight, that chilling series of shootings from New York to Missouri, and now Texas. Tonight, two cheerleaders outside Austin shot after one of them got into the wrong car in a grocery store parking lot. One of them in the ICU tonight. In upstate New York, the homeowner in court today after police say he shot and killed a young woman after the car she was in accidentally pulled into his driveway. Mireya Villarreal on the string of troubling shootings now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOMEOWNER PLEADS "NOT GUILTY"\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, tonight, news in the case of the black teenager who went to the wrong home to pick up his siblings shot in the head by that 84-year-old homeowner. That homeowner in court today and what played out. Alex Perez in Kansas City.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT DELAYS ABORTION PILL RULING\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The breaking news from the Supreme Court late today, extending women's access to the abortion pill for at least two more days. So, what happens after that? Rachel Scott reporting tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY PARKING GARAGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 In New York City, the video from inside the deadly parking garage collapse as that garage came crashing down. The new questions here tonight. Among them, the number of cars on that roof.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEAKED SECRETS INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts air national guardsman accused of leaking highly classified Pentagon documents in court today. We'll have the latest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRISIS IN SOUTH SUDAN\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Our reporting from South Sudan tonight, the urgent effort to get help to more than a million people. Families and children displaced by climate change, and you'll see it. And tonight, the key route in from Sudan halted after the deadly violence to the north that broke out while we were in the region. Tonight, what we witnessed on the ground firsthand, the staggering need and what you can do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORM THREAT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And here in the US, the severe storm threat as we come on the air tonight. Tornado watches across several states. Those storms across the Midwest then moving into the east.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight with David Muir."\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230420ej4j00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEADLY PARKING GARAGE COLLAPSE INVESTIGATION INTO BUILDING'S AGE AND WEIGHT LOAD\b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GILLIS, ROTH, RODRIGUEZ, MONAHAN\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, LESTER, YARL, MERRITT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOMEOWNER PLEADS NOT GUILTY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DELAY, CALIFF, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT DELAYS ABORTION PILL DECISION\par \par \uc2 GARAGE, COLLAPSE, TRAVLOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY PARKING GARAGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Here in New York City tonight, video inside that deadly parking garage collapse amid serious new questions. Tonight here, the images and the roar of the crash.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just incredible video, one person killed, several injured.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And tonight, those questions among them, the number of cars on the roof. Trevor Ault at the scene.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INVESTIGATION INTO BUILDING'S AGE AND WEIGHT LOAD\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, new video from inside that New York City parking garage capturing the thunderous moment it collapsed.\par \par \uc2 ANGELA TRAVLOS (NEIGHBOR)\par \par \uc2 My whole apartment shook like an earthquake.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The three-story structure pancaking cars piled on top of each other, killing one person, injuring seven other. Sources say the building manager was killed. Today, his body removed from the rubble. Neighbors tell us he was about to leave when the building collapsed. This giant crane pulling crushed cars out one by one, this SUV falling to the street. The building still unstable. Gas tanks and electric car batteries now at risk of exploding.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, we've learned investigators are focusing on the age of this near-century-old building and there's also questions about the weight on the roof. There were 50 cars on the top floor when the structure collapsed. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Trevor Ault in New York tonight. Thank you, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230420ej4j00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL BATTLE HEADS TO SUPREME COURT NEW PROTESTS AS JUSTICES SET TO DECIDE WHETHER TO TAKE UP CASE\b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE CHINESE SPY BALLOONS?\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, LEAK, FALLOUT, ARREST, INTEL, BLINKEN\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SEGREST, SWEET 16, VICTIMS, BURKETT, SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, DOMINION, FOX NEWS, DEFAMATION\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, CHAOS, SUDAN, CONTROL, PARTHASARATHY\par \par \uc2 YARL, SHOOTING, PROTESTS, LUCAS, GRAVES\par \par \uc2 BOSTON MARATHON, BOMBING, HONORING\par \par \uc2 STARSHIP, LIFTOFF, MUSK, INGRAM, MAEZAW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SAILING, SEARCH, O'BRIEN, GROSS, HIGGINS\par \par \uc2 LEE, MURDER, MOMENI, STABBING, MOTIVE, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 "LOVE IS BLIND", NETFLIX, REUNION, LIVE, GLITCHES\par \par \uc2 A.I., MUSIC, ARTISTS, COPYRIGHT, ROGERS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SEARCH, SEGREST, TAYLOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH FOR SWEET 16 SHOOTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST FOUR DEAD, MORE THAN TWO DOZEN INJURED AT ALABAMA PARTY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE HEADS TO SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW PROTESTS AS JUSTICES SET TO DECIDE WHETHER TO TAKE UP CASE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we have the latest on the battle over the abortion bill (sic). The Supreme Court set to weigh in this week as the Justice Department appeals rulings that would severely restrict the availability of the drug. Our senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott is in Washington with more. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you. The fate of the pill used in more than half of abortions in the United States is now in the hands of the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Over the weekend, protesters taking to the streets after two federal judges issued conflicting rulings on whether or not to ban the abortion drug mifepristone. The Supreme Court stepping in, putting all of this on hold for now, making the abortion drug mifepristone available at least until Wednesday, giving the justices more time to review this case and decide whether or not they want to take it up.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATES WITH NEAR TOTAL ABORTION BANS MAP\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade nearly a year ago, 14 states have stopped nearly all abortion services. But if the Supreme Court does decide to move forward with new restrictions on the abortion drug, this would apply to every single state in the nation, including the 36 states where abortion is currently legal and available.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICES' NEXT STEPS WILL DETERMINE PILL'S AVAILABILITY\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, this would change the landscape once again for women in this country nearly one year after Roe was overturned. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Huge implications there. All right, Rachel Scott, thanks for staying on this one for us.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230522ej4h0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL BATTLE BEFORE SUPREME COURT RULINGS DUE THIS WEEK ON OTHER MAJOR CASES\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, BIDEN, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 STORM, WEATHER, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER SWEEPS THROUGH HEARTLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 26 MILLION AMERICANS UNDER ALERT FOR SEVERE THUNDERSTORMS, DANGEROUS WINDS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE BEFORE SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RULINGS DUE THIS WEEK ON OTHER MAJOR CASES\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the major week ahead at the Supreme Court. The battle over the abortion pill front and center but rulings are due on other big issues. And ABC Jay O'Brien joins us now from the court with more. Jay, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio, good morning. There is this collective sense of legal limbo this morning, and the clock is ticking. The justices have until midnight Wednesday to rule on that abortion pill matter.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The case, the question that they're facing is somewhat narrow here. The court has to decide if mifepristone, the abortion pill, will be allowed to be available in its current form while a larger court case about the drugs approval by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  plays out in federal court. On Friday, Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  decided the drug can briefly stay available while he and the other justices make up their minds on that question. And the consequences here are stark. Abortion rights advocates estimate what's referred to as medication abortion makes up more than half of US abortions. At least four Democrat-led states have already begun to stockpile abortion medications, bracing for the court's ruling.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And all of this is turning national attention right back on to the Supreme Court, which has a 6-3 conservative majority, you'll remember, and overturned Roe v. Wade less than a year ago. There were protests in front of the Supreme Court and across the country yesterday ahead of this ruling.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICES ALSO SET TO HEAR CASES REGARDING FREE SPEECH & VOTING RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And no matter what happens with the abortion pill access availability ruling, that overall case, that larger federal case into the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval of mifepristone, that is expected to continue to drag on for weeks. And any ultimate decision there would likely be appealed right back here potentially to the Supreme Court, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Jay, I know you're looking into other big issues on the Supreme Court's plate this week. What are you seeing there?\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the justices are going to hear a case into religious accommodations at the workplace, which could have implications for workplaces across the country. And there's also a free speech case that they'll hear into \uc2 Facebook\uc2  messages sent by a convicted stalker. And they have some big decisions to make, too, into issues like voting rights and affirmative action. But those decisions aren't expected until closer toward the summer. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A big week at the Supreme Court. Jay O'Brien, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej4g0002w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 3,740 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM, TEIXEIRA, LEAK, GREENE, ABORTION, SCOTUS, SAUDI ARABIA\par \par \uc2 KLOBUCHAR, ABORTION PILL, SCOTUS, FEINSTEIN, KHANNA, THOMAS\par \par \uc2 MOORE, MD, ABORTION PILL, CRIME, SERVICE\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM JANUARY 18\par \par \uc2 2024, SCOTT, TRUMP, DESANTIS, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM WEDNESDAY\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TIM SCOTT (REP) (SOUTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 Today our country is once again being tested. Once again our divisions run deep and the threat to our future is real. That's why I'm announcing my exploratory committee for president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I will announce it relatively soon, but the trick here is just to reinforce my sense of optimism about what can be done. I told you my plan is to run again.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That was South Carolina Senator Tim Scott announcing a 2024 exploratory committee, and President Biden inching, it seemed a - a step closer to announcing his reelection during his visit to Ireland. Let's bring in the Roundtable. We have former New Jersey Governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , former DNC Chair Donna Brazile, "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " opinion contributor Jane Coaston, and "Politico Playbook" co-author Rachael Bade. So, Rachael, let me start with Tim Scott. I know you, you've got a lot of sources on Capitol Hill. It seems to me he's somebody who has a lot of friends in Congress, Republicans who don't like, who don't want Donald Trump to be the nominee again. They don't particularly like DeSantis. They wanted him to run.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIM SCOTT LAUNCHES 2024 PRESIDENTIAL EXPLORATORY COMMITTEE\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I mean, I think a lot of his colleagues are encouraging him to do so. He's got this, sort of, incredible story of someone who grew up in poverty and look at him now as a sitting senator. He, he's got Conservative policy chops, a very different tone than Donald Trump. He's considered very friendly, very good with voters in person.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 But I think, you know, if Republicans are being honest with themselves, it's a real question about whether or not Republican primary voters want a nice guy like that. And so, I think people want him to run for two reasons. Number one, someone just told me there's, quote, "no downside in running," right?\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 You could potentially be picked as a, as a vice presidential candidate running mate. The other issue that we could see this address is that if Trump is out there sort of taking, you know, swings at everybody, which he still is, I mean, he's doing this all the time, Scott offers a very different tone. And that's a tone that Republicans are hoping voters are sort of gonna listen to as well, and not alienating swing voters. But I think realistically, you know, Republicans will tell you he's probably not gonna be the nominee.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENCE GETS MIXED RECEPTION AT NRA CONVENTION\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and if you look, Governor Christie, this week we saw, we saw \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  get booed at the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2 . This is a guy arguably who is more pro-Second Amendment than Donald Trump and he gets booed by the, by the NRA. \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2  says he's not running. Glenn Youngkin, the Governor of Virginia, seems like he's certainly not running. I mean, is the field starting to look like Trump? I mean...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POMPEO WILL FORGO A '24 CAMPAIGN, YOUNGKIN SIGNALS THE SAME\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, no, I don't think it's a field starting to look like Trump. In fact, you know, when you're indicted in, in one place and, and you're facing investigations in two others, it makes you at least an uncertain winner.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But again, he's the, he's the former president, so of course he's gonna be the frontrunner. He has the best name ID in the race of anybody that's running, but you already have four other candidates now who are announced in. But this is what I said, Jon, a couple months ago on this, on this show. This is not going to be a 2016 field. This is gonna be six to eight candidates that are gonna be running. It'll be a normal type sized field. But certainly, it's not gonna be a field that Donald Trump has cleared.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because if you see, you know, already Asa Hutchison in the race, and Nikki Haley in the race, and now Tim Scott in the race, you know, these are substantial people who are gonna have something to say. And so, I don't think that's what it means at all. I do think each one of these decisions were made on rather personal levels. I think, in particular, Pompeo's was a decision that was just, he didn't wanna do it. And boy, you've got to really want to do this. Having done it, I can tell you, you've got to really want to do it...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Trump...\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...to be able to get in.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TO CARLSON: 'I'D NEVER DROP OUT'\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Trump, Trump had, had a very long interview with, with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . And he, Tucker asked him - directly, you know, will you run if you are not just indicted, but convicted? Here's what he had to say.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM TUESDAY\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Is there anything they could throw at you legally that would convince you to drop out of the race? If you get convicted in this case in New York, will you drop out?\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP (FORMER UNITED STATES PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 No, I'd never drop out. No, I'd never drop, it's not my thing. I wouldn't do it.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Not, not surprising, Donna.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, his legal troubles - those troubles have enabled him to solidify, I think, his base. And that is...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It boosted his fundraising.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Correct, 'cause was raising like $168,000 a day starting in January. And the day before he was indicted, his fundraising numbers have gone up. Now, we don't know the actual picture because we haven't seen the report yet. But look, 72 percent of Republican voters, 72 percent of Republican voters believe that Donald Trump has had a positive impact on the Republican Party. Seventy-nine percent of Republicans, this is a Quinnipiac poll. Don't, it didn't come from my household. Seventy-nine percent of Republicans voters see themselves as members of the MAGA movement.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, it doesn't matter the size, Governor Christie. And I don't know if you're getting into the pool. But if you are, you need to jump in really quick. Because there's a, a Republican debate coming up in a few months and you're going to have to raise a lot of money, well, get 40,000 donors. But the Republican...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got some, you got some advice here, right at the Roundtable.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All for free too, it's really great.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I'm - trying to advise him, if you're gonna leave me, you've got to leave me quick, okay? But, but the Republican Party has, is, is going to solidify around Donald Trump during this first period. But I think if somebody can make a good case against Donald Trump, then you'll see more people jumping in before the end of the summer.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and we're gonna get Governor Christie to respond to that. But first, Jane, I mean, the, the question is, if it's not Trump, who is it?\par \par \uc2 JANE COASTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think that, that is, one, it is April of 2023.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. Yes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IS TRUMP THE CLEAR GOP FRONTRUNNER?\par \par \uc2 JANE COASTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I would like us all to remember that it is April of the year before the presidential election. There's a lot we don't know. I am already seeing pieces about how Governor DeSantis is retooling a campaign that has not technically begun. So, I just, I, I really...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It sort of looks like it's begun.\par \par \uc2 JANE COASTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sort of. But you, you know, you see him in New Hampshire, and he's kind of, he's learning how to walk and talk to people like a member of the human race. But you're also seeing people who are criticizing the very things that people voted for him to do. For instance, the six-week abortion ban in Florida which Republicans very much wanted him to do. And you're seeing that a bunch of other Republicans are saying, "No, no, don't do this. We talk about this, but we don't actually do it."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESANTIS SIGNS 6-WEEK ABORTION BAN IN FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 JANE COASTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so, I think that it is, that if it's, if it's not Trump, it is likely to be DeSantis. But I think that the challenge is that the Republican primary audience and the audience of people who vote for the presidents are two very different audiences. As Donna was saying, what Republican primary voters want and what the American voter at large want are two very different things.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 JANE COASTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Some people are going to want \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . But I think that on a national level, what - \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ' policies play as is going to be very different from what they look like in Florida.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, so I want to ask you about the abortion thing, but first, do you want to make some news today about your plans for 2024?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm, I'm with Donna this morning, and I'm staying with Donna this morning.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, okay, so no announcement now. So, what, so DeSantis signed this six-week abortion ban, signed it at night. I mean, I've seen him do live on Fox News, bill signings. This was, you know, a little photo leased at night. And then he went to \uc2 Liberty University\uc2  for - a speech, \uc2 Liberty University\uc2 , and he didn't even mention what he had just signed. So, I mean, what, how does this play out?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look, I've been saying for years as someone who is pro-life, that the way these decisions should be made is state by state. That they shouldn't be federalized in any way. That if you care about the Constitution, you believe in the Constitution, this is one that should be made state by state, so states are making these decisions. So, in Florida, there's now a six-week ban. In New Jersey, you can have an abortion up to the ninth month. You're gonna see this across the country. There are going to be differences.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But does, does this hurt DeSantis as a presidential candidate, to be on the...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POST-ROE POLITICS RAISE NEW QUESTIONS FOR PRESIDENTIAL HOPEFULS\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It will only...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...(inaudible) side of this.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Listen, anything will hurt any candidate if they don't have a believable explanation for why they did what they did.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What voters want more than anything else is for you to be authentic. They're willing to disagree with you, most voters, not all, but most. Look, I was a pro-life governor in New Jersey, which is one of the most pro-choice states in America, and I got elected and reelected with 61 percent of the vote, right? So, people make this information...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you weren't attempting to ban abortion in New Jersey?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I wasn't. But - Jon, point is I...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Your personal views were, I mean...\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was very clear about my personal views, though. And - what people, if people believe it comes from your heart and that have a legitimate, not a political explanation for what you're doing, lots of people, not all voters, but lots of voters will say to you, all right, we can disagree on that one. What else are you for or against?\par \par \uc2 JANE COASTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But I think people believe in his heart. I think what people don't necessarily believe in is \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ' commitment to federalism. I think we've seen with Lindsey Graham attempting to come up with federal legislation regarding a 15-week ban, and you, you heard this from Conservatives even before Roe, Roe went down, that it would be sent back to the states. States could make the decision. And now you're hearing from a lot of Conservatives, "Well, actually..."\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But I think that's wrong, Jane. I agree with you. I think it's wrong. I think if, our position for 50 years, as Conservatives, post-Roe, has been this should be a decision that's made by the states. And I think if you deviate from that, you undercut the credibility of the position you've taken for 50 years. So, you and I agree on that one. It should be - it should be consistent.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCOTUS TO HEAR CASE ON ABORTION PILL ACCESS, FDA AUTHORITY\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, but the medical community is very alarmed by this decision to sort of dictate how we're going to treat people who are, you know, have an, whether it's an abortion or whether it's some other medical issue. I think at, at the heart of this conversation, with the, with the, with the abortion pill is whether or not we're going to allow politicians to pretend to be doctors, and, and, and...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Judges, in this case a judge.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A judge, who's not a doctor, to say that this meditation is somehow or another unsafe and should be restricted or not available. This is, this going to be a liability to the Republicans, not just in the general election, but as you've seen in states, just this recent case in - Wisconsin where you had two, with the state Supreme Court case, I've got so much on my mind about it. I am so angry about what's happening.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, calm down.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm angry because of what it's doing to women in this country. I'm angry because it is, it's, put, setting us back. I'm also angry because once again men are telling us what to do with our bodies. And it's time they stop and understand the ramifications and the repercussions of this. That's why I'm angry about it.\par \par \uc2 JANE COASTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think the most important political priority for any political party is to not be the people telling people what to do. For the last five years, we've heard from Republicans, especially even during COVID, about how freedom was going to reign and that they were just gonna let people make decisions for themselves. They want to be the cool mom of politics. Well, that era has ended. And I think that there is a specific type of libertarianism that is very popular in America, unlike the Libertarian Party.\par \par \uc2 JANE COASTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But I, there's a specific type of "don't tell me what to do. Let me make my decisions. Let me make my decisions for my family," that is very politically profitable. And I think that if Democrats are able to say that "we are the party that says you can make these decisions, you can make decisions for your family, your family can make decisions for themselves," I think that will be politically profitable. And I think that for Republicans, it's going to be challenging to - try to sound simultaneously like cool mom and the moral majority that so many of us grew up with.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And...\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, the Democratic Party is all for that on abortion, but they are against it when it comes to public education. When it comes to public education, people shouldn't be able to make their own decisions. You shouldn't be able to have the ability to go, have your child go to parochial school if you can't afford it, or to go to a charter school if they're not available in your town, or to able to decide what your children should be able to learn about sexuality and what age they should learn that.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, the Democrats are gonna have a hard time making that case when you look at public education and what their position is, which is, us and the teachers union know what to tell your children...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But...\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...and where they should go to school and how they should be taught.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) public education should be accessible and safe.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But - Rachael, but, but Rachael, on, on the question of abortion, the polling suggests there's been quite a shift in this country, in which used to be, you know, pretty close to 50/50 on the abortion issue, is now, you know, very much in - favor of abortion rights. The number, the percentage of people that really want to have severe restrictions on abortions is actually clearly in the minority. Isn't this a - general election problem for Republicans?\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, I think there's no doubt about it. I was just looking at polling over this weekend. I think it, it was saying 63 percent of Americans disagree with this five-week abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 Like, after five weeks you can't get an abortion. And that's gonna be a problem for DeSantis, in that, yes, he can make this argument that okay, the states all are going to make their own decisions here. It's not for the federal government to say. The states will be the ones to decide. But, you know, he's gonna face questions about, okay, if he signed this and you thought it was good for Florida, are you saying it's good for Florida but it's not good for the United States?\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 So, how do you, how do you sort of justify having two different positions on this? Or is he gonna say everybody should have a five and six-week abortion ban, which obviously is really unpopular. So, I mean, it, the politics of this are very difficult, and that's why you saw him signing this bill in the middle of the night. And regarding Senator Tim Scott, I mean, he's somebody who was just was asked about this, what, the day after he said he was having this presidential test run.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 And he, he couldn't answer the question. He didn't know where to, where to respond and eventually had to put out a statement...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He said he the most Conservative...\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 ...saying 20 weeks. Yes.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He wants the most Conservative position and then...\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...then he put out another statement. Look...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Saying 20 week-ban (inaudible)...\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (POLITICO PLAYBOOK CO-AUTHOR)\par \par \uc2 Twenty weeks.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, right, to criminalize women. It's just wrong. To - put women in this position across the country, is just immoral, and it's wrong and it's unjustified.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, how do they answer, I tried to, you know, I've tried to address this with Lindsey Graham, but how do they address the judicial activism part of this? I mean, a judge, an unelected judge in Amarillo, Texas making the policy on, on FDA approval?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look, I, I think the Supreme Court, when you look back at their, their decisions in this area, I think the Conservatives on the Supreme Court may have trouble with this one. Because their attitude has been on issues of technical, medical judgment or other types of technical judgments that they defer to the regulatory agencies. Now, while Conservatives on the Court have said they think regulatory agencies have too much reach, that's a different argument...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...than the argument of there's substantive expertise. So, this is gonna be an interesting one to watch.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And (inaudible) all right, we're out of time. Coming up, a closer look into the fight for clean drinking water in the United States. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230421ej4g00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ONE-ON-ONE WITH SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM SUSPECT IN PENTAGON INTEL LEAK, 21-YEAR-OLD AIRMAN ARRESTED\b0\par\par\uc2 1,939 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM, TEIXEIRA, LEAK, GREENE, ABORTION, SCOTUS, SAUDI ARABIA\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's dig into all of this with Republican Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 . Senator Graham joins us from Jerusalem. Thank you for joining us. You're gonna get a, a senators-only briefing, all-senators briefing on this extraordinary leak. What questions are you gonna be asking the administration?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT IN PENTAGON INTEL LEAK, 21-YEAR-OLD AIRMAN, ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 How a 21-year-old airman at the Massachusetts Air National Guard could have access to all this information? Why did he do it and what is the damage assessment? I've been to Saudi Arabia. I'm in Israel. I can promise you it's been very damaging. There's information about \uc2 Mossad\uc2  supposedly helping the protesters. There's information about the air defense capability of Ukraine. And everybody in the region's really worried because who wants to share information with the United States if you're gonna read about it in the paper or find it on the Internet? So, this has done a lot of damage to us in the region.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, I mean, you, you were an Air National Guardsman. Are you surprised that a, that a, such a junior Air National Guardsman had access to this kind of information?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 I was a captain and a major. I would be surprised if I had that kind of information. Yes, the system failed. This is a major failure. And those who are trying to sugar coat this on the right, you cannot allow a single individual of the military intelligence community to leak classified information because they disagree with policy. I don't know what led to this airman's actions, but he's done a lot of damage to our standing.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 It's very hard to get people to come forward right now to tell us about things we need to know about if they feel like they're gonna be compromised. The sources and methods we collect on adversaries have been compromised. And I am stunned that somebody at that level could have so much access. So, the question is, how did he get it and why did he do it? And we, some people need to be fired over this.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, as you mentioned it, there are some on the right that are not only sugar coating it, but actually applauding him. I mean...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...take, take a look at what \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  tweeted.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REP \uc2 MARJORIE TAYLOR GREENE\uc2  DEFENDS ALLEGED PENTAGON LEAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF TWEET\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She said, "Jack Teixeira is white, male, Christian, and anti-war. That makes him an enemy to the Biden regime. And he told the truth about troops being on the ground in Ukraine and a lot more." I mean, Tucker Carlson's kind of turning him into a hero. What, what do you make of that? Why?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 What they're suggesting will destroy America's ability to defend itself, that it's okay to release classified information based on your political views, that the ends justify the means. It is not okay. If you're a member of the military intelligence community and you disagree with American policy and you think you're gonna be okay when it comes to leaking classified information, you're gonna go to jail. It's one of the most irresponsible statements you can make. The ability for America to gather intelligence from human resources on the ground has been compromised.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 We can't have a chaotic intelligence gathering system. If you give us information and it's disclosed, you can lose your life. The way we gather intelligence protects our country. There are military members serving today from Georgia and other places who are less safe because of what this airman did. There is no justification for this. And for any member of Congress to suggest it's okay to leak classified information because you agree with the cause is terribly irresponsible and puts America in serious danger.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT CONSIDERING CASE TO LIMIT ABORTION PILL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, - let's turn to the confusion over the various rulings on, on the abortion pill. I've heard you for years rail against judicial activism, saying that, you know, judges shouldn't be basically legislating from the bench. So what do you make of this? A single judge from Texas...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...singlehandedly upending the legal status of, of the abortion pill?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I don't like a district court judge issuing a national decree, even if I agree with the judge. And what the judge held here is that the Federal Drug Administration didn't follow their own rules. So, the Biden administration is trying to send the abortion pill through the mail. There's a statute on the books called the Comstock Act that prohibits sending abortion materials through the mail. That's gonna go all the way to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 So, I think the radical abortion policies of the Biden administration are wrong. But, at the end of the day, we're a rule of law nation, and let's see what the Supreme Court does with this. But the decision by the Biden administration, Jonathan, to allow the pill to be sent through the mail violates an existing statute on the books.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOV. DESANTIS SIGNS 6-WEEK ABORTION BAN IN FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What do you make of Florida? DeSantis has now signed a six-week ban. Is that gonna complicate his efforts to become president of the United States should he become a candidate? To have a six-week ban, that's far more...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 I think he...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...aggressive than what you've proposed.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Right. So, the, the, under my legislation, states can be more restrictive, but at 15 weeks, we limit abortion on demand. My Democratic colleagues (inaudible) said, they have supported legislation allowing abortion on demand, taxpayer funded, up at the moment of birth. DeSantis will have to ask the question, answer the question, do you support a national ban at six weeks? Why did you pick six weeks? The legislative body of Florida supported what he did.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 This is an issue worth talking about. Should we be a nation that allows abortion on demand up to the moment of birth with taxpayer-funded money? Or, should we have limits at 15 weeks like Europe? Should we be like North Korea and China, or should we be more like Europe nationally? Should states have a right to regulate abortion up to a point? These are issues that matter.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Should young girls be able to play sports with biological males? The policy of the Biden administration is to allow young children, minor children to transition, to have their lives upside down to allow medical procedures to change gender before, before you get 18 years of age. All of these issues will be on the ballot, and they should be.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GRAHAM MEETS WITH SAUDI CROWN PRINCE HE ONCE CONDEMNED\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Senator, you were just in Saudi Arabia. You met with Crown Prince Mohammad bin Salman, MBS, as he is known.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But - I remember how highly critical you were of him after...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...after the murder of Jamal Khashoggi, "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " columnist.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 You're right. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's take a listen to what you had to say back in 2018.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM OCTOBER 2018\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 I can never do business with Saudi Arabia again until we get this behind us.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Right. And what does that mean?\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM DECEMBER 2018\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 That means I'm not going back to Saudi Arabia as long as this guy's in charge. The Crown Prince is a wrecking ball. I think the behavior before the Khashoggi murder was beyond disturbing, and I cannot see him being a reliable partner to the United States.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So you said he was beyond toxic. You would never return to Saudi while he was in charge.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So what happened? What changed?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Right. Well, a couple things happened. Number one, I've been talking with the Biden administration about working with Saudi Arabia to build on the reforms they're doing in their country and to build on the Abraham Accords. If you get nothing else out of this interview, things in Saudi Arabia are changing very quickly for the better. I see a chance to normalize the relationship between the United States, Saudi Arabia and Israel that would be transformative for the region.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Saudi Arabia purchased $36 billion worth of 737 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  jets made in Charleston, South Carolina. They picked the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  787 over the Airbus. I came over here to say thanks to Saudi Arabia. They're thinking about buying more jets, and I also came over to, to them to caution them about getting too cozy with China and Iran. But Vision 2030 of the crown prince is real. Women can drive for the first time in modern Saudi history. Women can go out to dinner without a male escort.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM (REP-SC) (RANKING MEMBER JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 His vision for the country economically is transformative. A trillion dollars is gonna be spent to modernize Saudi Arabia. I'd like to be part of that transition. What I saw in Saudi Arabia was a game changer for me. I want to build on the progress, but I want to have an honest, candid relationship. There are things that need to change in Saudi Arabia. But Jonathan, the ability to work with Saudi Arabia is at an all-time high. If we could normalize a relationship with Saudi Arabia, and then Israel, build upon the Abraham Accords, it'd be the best thing I have seen in my lifetime, regarding Mideast security and America's security.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Senator Graham, thank you for joining us.\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230421ej4g00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "THE POWER OF WATER" SERIES "OUR AMERICA: TROUBLE ON TAP"\b0\par\par\uc2 888 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM, TEIXEIRA, LEAK, GREENE, ABORTION, SCOTUS, SAUDI ARABIA\par \par \uc2 KLOBUCHAR, ABORTION PILL, SCOTUS, FEINSTEIN, KHANNA, THOMAS\par \par \uc2 MOORE, MD, ABORTION PILL, CRIME, SERVICE\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM JANUARY 18\par \par \uc2 2024, SCOTT, TRUMP, DESANTIS, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM WEDNESDAY\par \par \uc2 NC, WATER, PFAS, \uc2 EPA\uc2 , REGAN, OLINGER, OLSON, DONOVAN, CHEMOUR\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM MARCH 14\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL REGAN\uc2  (EPA ADMINISTRATOR)\par \par \uc2 Very proud to announce in Wilmington, North Carolina, \uc2 EPA\uc2 's first national standard to regulate PFAs, the forever chemical compound that has been linked to cancer, to high cholesterol and other serious illnesses. \uc2 EPA\uc2 's priority is protecting communities. Everyone deserves clean air to breathe and clean water to drink.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 EPA\uc2 's announcement last month to strengthen drinking water standards brought a sigh of relief to one community in North Carolina that's been living with chemicals that are associated with serious health problems. Residents of the region shared their story with ABC News, National Geographic and our ABC-owned television stations.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 CARROL OLINGER (FAYETTEVILLE NC RESIDENT AND ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 I didn't know I was drinking poisonous water. I didn't know when I was coming home from a long day at work and I needed to fill up my jug, I'm still drinking poisonous water. My name is Carrol Olinger. I've lived in Fayetteville, Hope Mills since 1995.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAYETTEVILLE, NORTH CAROLINA, WHERE THE CHEMOURS PLANT IS LOCATED, IS ONE OF THE MOST DISADVANTAGED COMMUNITIES IN THE UNITED STATES, ACCORDING TO CENSUS DATA FROM THE WHITE HOUSE COUNCIL ON ENVIRONMENTAL QUALITY.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IT FACES HIGH RATE OF POLLUTION, HEALTH RISKS, AND POVERTY.\par \par \uc2 ERIK D OLSON (SENIOR STRATEGIST \uc2 NATURAL RESOURCES DEFENSE COUNCIL\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, safe drinking water in the United States sometimes depends on your zip code. We should not have to worry rely on being wealthy or in a community that happens to have a lot of resources in order to have water that's safe. In low-income communities, in communities of color, in Native American communities, we're seeing that they do not have safe drinking water, and that needs to be fixed.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 49% OF ZIP CODES WHERE PFAS ARE DETECTED IN WATER SITES ARE IN ZIP CODES WHERE THE MEDIAN HOUSEHOLD INCOME WAS BELOW THE 2020 NATIONAL AVERAGE OF $67,521.\par \par \uc2 CARROL OLINGER (FAYETTEVILLE NC RESIDENT AND ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 I call myself an accidental activist. What do we want?\par \par \uc2 CLEAN WATER ACTIVISTS (NORTH CAROLINA RESIDENTS)\par \par \uc2 Clean water!\par \par \uc2 CARROL OLINGER (FAYETTEVILLE NC RESIDENT AND ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 When do we want it?\par \par \uc2 CLEAN WATER ACTIVISTS (NORTH CAROLINA RESIDENTS)\par \par \uc2 Now!\par \par \uc2 CARROL OLINGER (FAYETTEVILLE NC RESIDENT AND ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 I don't think that I was a cheerleader for environmental justice, environmental health, but I think I am now because of the situation I accidentally fell into. Unfortunately, it's hurting communities that look like me, underserved communities. I think that the Black and Brown, Latino, Indian communities, when it hits fully, it's gonna hurt them the most because they're not gonna have an option. It's scary.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DONOVAN (CO-FOUNDER CLEAN CAPE FEAR)\par \par \uc2 We don't need incremental action. We need strong, forceful responses that can correct 40 years of damage and 40 years of neglect.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL REGAN\uc2  (EPA ADMINISTRATOR)\par \par \uc2 President Biden took this issue very serious from day one. My name is \uc2 Michael Regan\uc2 . I'm the Administrator of the \uc2 United States Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 . Prior to this position, I was Secretary of the Environment for the state of North Carolina. Very early in my tenure, we found out that a company was discharging PFAs into the Cape Fear River, a source of water for hunting, for fishing and for recreation. And so, yes, my experience with PFAs was stark.\par \par \uc2 EMILY DONOVAN (CO-FOUNDER CLEAN CAPE FEAR)\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EPA\uc2  is saying we'll address your requests, but we're gonna address them through our national testing strategy. You know what I'm not seeing in those testing strategies? I'm not seeing the chemicals that are actually in my blood.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL REGAN\uc2  (EPA ADMINISTRATOR)\par \par \uc2 The previous administration didn't put actions in place to develop the sound science to develop very strong regulations, and so from day one, we took that mission on very seriously. And so, my attitude is the same as \uc2 EPA\uc2  administrator as it was as state secretary. Hold corporate polluters accountable and work towards regulations that make it very clear what is safe and what is not safe.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AS NORTH CAROLINA'S SECRETARY OF THE ENVIRONMENT, REGAN FINED THE POLLUTER, THE CHEMOUS COMPANY, $12-MILLION IN 2018 FOR VIOLATING THE CLEAN WATER LAWS.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE COMPANY DID NOT ADMIT TO ANY VIOLATIONS, BUT AGREED TO TERMS WITH THE STATE TO AVOID FURTHER LITIGATION.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OUR AMERICA: TROUBLE ON TAP\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "Our America: Trouble on Tap" premieres April 21st at OurAmericaABC.com and on Hulu on April 22nd. You can catch more of ABC's climate and environmental reporting all this week as part of our ongoing series "The Power of Water." We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That's all for today. Thank you for sharing part of your Sunday with us. Check out "World News Tonight," and have a great day.\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230421ej4g00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAYOR WES MOORE MARYLAND AMONG STATES RACING TO STOCKPILE ABORTION MEDICINE\b0\par\par\uc2 2,008 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM, TEIXEIRA, LEAK, GREENE, ABORTION, SCOTUS, SAUDI ARABIA\par \par \uc2 KLOBUCHAR, ABORTION PILL, SCOTUS, FEINSTEIN, KHANNA, THOMAS\par \par \uc2 MOORE, MD, ABORTION PILL, CRIME, SERVICE\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM JANUARY 18\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Today is the opportunity. It is our opportunity to lead with love. It is our opportunity to create with compassion. It's our opportunity to fight fearlessly for our future. Maryland, our time is right now. Our time is now to build a state that for those who came before us that they fought for, and it's a state that leaves no one behind.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Democrat Wes Moore is an Army veteran, Rhodes scholar, a former investment banker, and former head of a nonprofit organization, and as of three months ago, the Governor of Maryland. Taking the oath of office on a Bible that once belonged to Frederick Douglas, he became his state's first Black governor in January. Governor Moore joins us now. Thank you for being here.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 It's my pleasure. Great to be with you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK: EXCLUSIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARYLAND AMONG STATES RACING TO STOCKPILE ABORTION MEDICINE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So - I want to start with, with the news of, of the, the abortion pill status being very much in doubt. You announced late Friday that Maryland will be stockpiling Mifepristone? What, what's your thinking on this?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Well, my, my thinking is Maryland's gonna lead on this. You know, we, this is the first time that we've actually seen a Supreme Court - actively working to take rights away from people. Maryland is gonna be a state where we are going to protect reproductive health and reproductive rights. And, you know, not only have I instructed our Department of Health to be able to make this decision that we are going to be stockpiling the drug for, for upwards of three years, also, if you look at the legislative session that we just had, we passed three bills that was focusing on things like increasing access, increasing privacy, and also making sure that when people come to Maryland, they're not gonna be criminalized.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 And I worked in partnership and supported the legislature's leadership of the presiding officers to make sure that next year abortion and reproductive rights will be on the ballot in the state of Maryland. So, Maryland is going to lead on this issue.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS PRIORITIZE FIGHTING CRIME AMID GOP ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And in your inaugural address, you - addressed the issue of crime, which, of course, is a big issue especially in - Baltimore, but throughout Maryland. You said, "We do not have to choose between a safe state and a just state. And Maryland can and will be both." So, what, you're, you're in, I guess, you're, you're about 89 days in?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 That's right.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What - is your approach to, to dealing with the issue of, of criminal justice?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Well, you know, you think, in Maryland, for the past eight years in the state of Maryland, we've watched the homicide rate double in the state of Maryland.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They have what, 355 murders in Baltimore?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 In - in Baltimore city alone, right?\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 And in the, and in the state you've seen the level of nonfatal shootings in the state of Maryland over the past eight years. It has doubled. And so, we ran on the idea that we are going to take this seriously and we're gonna move aggressively. And it was going to be an all-of-the-above approach. I mean, just last night in Baltimore we had a 12-year-old murdered with an assault rifle. A 12-year-old.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 And so, when we talk about an all-of-the-above approach it's why, in our first 90 days, yes, we did things like invest a historic measure of $107 million into mental and behavioral health support, that we put, that we put $122 million into local law enforcement to include $17.5 million into Baltimore city alone. But it's also about...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So - you're (inaudible) really not in Defund the Police mode?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 No, not at all. And - also, when you look at the fact that, if you think about how we're actually investing in other things as well, because you're not going to militarize your way out with something that is a larger challenge. We have to get these illegal guns off of our streets. And at the same time, it's the reason that we made record investment in public education. It's the reason that we also did things like investing in, in a service year option where high school grads will have a chance to have a year of service to the state of Maryland. So, this is an all of the - all-the-above approach in the way that we're looking at public safety.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOORE'S YEAR OF SERVICE PLAN PASSES MARYLAND LEGISLATURE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was struck by something else you said in your inaugural address. You talked about having handcuffs on your wrists at, at 11 years old.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible). Tell me that story.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLITICAL NEWCOMER MOORE ON HIS FUTURE IN OFFICE\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 I, when I was 11 years old was when I felt handcuffs.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 And, and I, and I, I thought about it in the moment of the inauguration where, if someone would've said to that 11-year-old kid with handcuffs on his wrists, the child of an immigrant single mother...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 ...who was just trying to find his way, and if someone would've said to that kid, you know, one day you could be governor, I would've never believed them. All...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what happened? What, what, why did you have handcuffs on your wrists...\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Well, so, so in that, in that case it was because I was spray painting and- trying to leave my mark on the world by a spray paint can.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 But I figured, and the thing that happened to me was, people showed me that there was another way to leave your mark on the world.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 And it wasn't spray paint cans. It was actually being part of something bigger than yourself. And so, I had the opportunity, despite having a lot of challenges when I was young. My dad died when I was young, in front of me. I had the opportunity to go on and I joined the Army when I was 17 years old. I, I ended up deploying overseas, running a small business, and then running one of the largest poverty fighting organizations in this country.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 And the reason that I wanted to run for governor in the first place, is I said, we can actually build a new type ecosystem of politics in our state, and one that says this is not about how we're going to exclude, but how we're going to include and it's gonna create a better path for each and every one of us.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and you, you've talked a lot about service, and I think it's, it's your, the first of your four pillars you talk about, a year of public service available for every high school graduate before either college or, or going to work. Public service is something, national service is something we've heard for years political leaders talk about. You know, George W. Bush, George H. W. Bush was with his thousand points of light.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 That's right.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 ...AmeriCorps\uc2 , - Governor Hogan talked about this. How are you actually gonna make that happen?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Well, we already...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How do you pay for it?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 We already did.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, yeah, for two - what's it, for 200 people for the initial...\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Well, well, so what's, so what's gonna happen is, Maryland is now, in our first 90 days...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 ...Maryland's now the first state in the country to offer a service year option for high school graduates. And really what it is, is that for, when a person graduates from high school, they can join the military, they can join the workforce, they can go to trade school. You know, they can, they can, you know, they can, there's a few different options. But what Maryland is now doing is, Maryland's now saying, or you could have a year of service to the state, and partnering with local nonprofits, - you know, companies, also labor unions. And we're really doing it for, for three different reasons.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 One is we believe that service is generally sticky, and those who serve together generally stay together. The second, this is about experiential learning and giving young people a chance to learn more about the different options that are available for them to be able to do. And, and the third reason is this is gonna redefine patriotism in the state of Maryland. When people talk about what does it mean being a patriot, being a patriot, it means lifting your neighbors up and not tearing them down.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How, how do, just...\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 And that's what we're gonna do.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...just quickly, how do you pay for it? 'Cause it sounds expensive to have every, every high school graduate would have a year, a year...\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How, how do they get paid? How does it work?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 They would have a year of service, and at the end of the year, they would actually receive a $3,000 stipend. And, and what we did was, not only did we allocate a portion for the state budget, but, also this being done in partnership with our federal partners, with \uc2 AmeriCorps\uc2 , with the private sector. Watching the level of engagement that we have already seen since the bill passage...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 ...has been phenomenal. And this is gonna have a market and a generational impact on the state of Maryland.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Governor Wes Moore, a lot, a lot more to talk about, but we got a start. Thank you very much for joining us.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 It's my pleasure. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Appreciate it. Coming up, significant new developments in the 2024 presidential race this week. We'll discuss it with the Roundtable right after the break.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Roundtable's up next. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230421ej4g00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THIS WEEK WITH GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS\b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "This week with George Stephanopoulos" starts right now.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Supreme showdown.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 When you attack the rights of women in America, you are attacking America.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court temporarily restores access to a widely used abortion pill, after a Texas judge suspended FDA approval.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM) (MASSACHUSETTS)\par \par \uc2 Abortion will remain safe, legal and accessible.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Democratic governors race to stock pile the drug, as Republicans in Florida enact a six week abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE JENNIFER CANADY (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 We are strengthening the culture of life in the state of Florida.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Intelligence scramble.\par \par \uc2 BRIGADIER GENERAL PATRICK RYDER (PENTAGON PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 This was a deliberate, criminal act.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A 21-year-old airman arrested and charged, accused of leaking military secrets. Why did the leak go undetected for so long? How damaging was it to national security?\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 New contender.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TIM SCOTT (REP) (SOUTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 America is starving for positive, optimistic leadership.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Senator Tim Scott moves towards a 2024 presidential bid, as Donald Trump vows to stay in the race, even if convicted.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP (FORMER UNITED STATES PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 I'd never drop, it's not my thing. I wouldn't do it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEN. \uc2 LINDSEY GRAHAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEN. AMY KLOBUCHAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOV. WES MOORE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We cover it all this morning with our headliners, Republican Lindsey Graham, Democrat Amy Klobuchar and Maryland Governor Wes Moore, plus analysis from our Powerhouse Roundtable.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News, it's "This Week." Here now, \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to "This Week."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last year, the Court said that the legal status of abortion should not be determined by unelected judges. As Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  wrote in the Majority's Opinion, quote, "It is time to heed the Constitution and return the issue of abortion to the people's elected representatives." Nearly a year later, the Court is once again at the center of the national debate over abortion, in a position to determine the fate of the most common form of abortion in the United States, the abortion pill Mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The pill has been legally available for some 23 years, but a decision by a federal judge in Texas aimed to change that, not just in Texas but throughout the United States. Justice Alito issued an 11th hour stay Friday that will leave the availability of the pill unchanged, but only until Wednesday, as the Court decides whether to intervene on lower court rulings that would either curtail access to the drug or make it illegal to manufacture and distribute it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll cover all the angles of the fast moving development in just a few minutes. But we begin with the fallout of the arrest of 21-year-old National Guardsman Jack Teixeira for allegedly leaking a treasure trove of classified material.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEAKED CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Teixeira has been charged with violating the Espionage Act for allegedly sharing hundreds of classified documents on Discord. That's an online server popular with young gamers. The disclosures included secret US military assessments and revealed just how closely the US monitors our rivals and our allies. The leaks also raised major questions. How did classified documents circulate online for months without the Pentagon's knowledge? Why did a young IT specialist have access to so many closely guarded secrets? And is the leak now contained?\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230421ej4g00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ONE-ON-ONE WITH SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY RESTORES ABORTION PILL ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,714 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM, TEIXEIRA, LEAK, GREENE, ABORTION, SCOTUS, SAUDI ARABIA\par \par \uc2 KLOBUCHAR, ABORTION PILL, SCOTUS, FEINSTEIN, KHANNA, THOMAS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And here now is Democratic Senator Amy Klobuchar. Thank you for being here, Senator Klobuchar. Let's start...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY RESTORES ABORTION PILL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Thanks, Jonathan.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's start with the, the abortion ruling. The Supreme Court has now issued this stay, but it's only until Wednesday. How, how do you expect this to play out?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 To me this is unbelievable. This is a drug that has been on the market for over 20 years. FDA does thorough review, finds it safe. You've got it safe in 60 countries. It's used in over half of the abortions. One judge from Amarillo, Texas, two judges on the 5th Circuit, all of them Trump appointed, should not be making a decision for women across the country. What is it gonna be next? Is that judge gonna not like birth control pills? Are we gonna have a judge who doesn't like Lipitor?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 There is a reason that Congress gave the FDA the power to make these decisions about safety. So, this is coming up before the Supreme Court. The Justice Department is aggressively pursuing this case. And as it is right now, literally these judges decided, well, you're not gonna be able to take it up to ten weeks. We think it's better to do seven weeks. Well, you can't get it in a pharmacy and you can't get it by the mail, so good luck.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what do you expect this court to do, the Supreme Court? Will they uphold?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think this one is really interesting because they have interpreted what we call standing, the ability to sue pretty narrowly at times. And in this case, you have the \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  way out there, not a radical group...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 ...saying this drug is safe. Then you have this small amount of people that brought this suit and they're claiming, oh, this is stressful for us 'cause it's against our morals. Okay, fine. But that is not the standard for standing to bring a suit. You've got to show harm or the expectation of some harm. And I can tell you who's harmed by this. It's women that are gonna have to take a bus across the country, from Texas to Minnesota or to Illinois. That's the problem right now.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and if the Court does uphold this, what are your options?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COULD CONGRESS PRESERVE ABORTION PILL ACCESS?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, the first one is to continue to aggressively litigate it. Remember, there's another case out of Washington state...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Washington.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 ...that applies to 17 states including my state, that it's also gonna work its way up to the court, so they're ultimately gonna make the decision. So, this is about the stay during that time. So, aggressive litigation. The second thing is realizing where the voters of this country are the - 70 to 80 percent are with us. The Republican Party, however, is not backing down. It is doubling down, putting in six-week abortion bans in, in Florida. What you've seen with criminalizing women, trying to criminalize doctors, this is an outrageous position for them to take. So ultimately, yes, this will get resolved state by state, but it's gonna get resolved at the ballot box in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, this'll be a central issue in 2024?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Yes, it will.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEN FEINSTEIN FACING PRESSURE TO RESIGN AMID HEALTH ISSUES\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, I want to ask you about one of your colleagues on the Judiciary Committee, - Senator Diane Feinstein. She has not voted since February 16th. She is suffering from shingles right now. Is, is her absence in such a closely divided Senate hurting you?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think she made the right decision to step off the Judiciary Committee. I serve on that committee. And we cannot advance judges or legislation with a missing person because of the close vote. So basically, in the next week or so, you're gonna see Senator Schumer, probably sooner than later, putting forward a name. And then the Senate, as they've done in the past, can vote to put this person on unanimously. That's what happened when you had \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2  resigning to run for office.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you, you don't think Republicans are gonna try to block that?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 I don't know. I sure hope not because that is against the precedent of the Senate and how we run things. But that's the first thing, so she did the right thing. As for the long term, many people have been out, as you know, for periods of time when they're sick and they have come back. In this case, we are gonna need her vote on the Senate floor eventually. We have things like the debt ceiling coming up. But I think what we need to do is take her at her word, she is recovering from shingles, and make sure she comes back.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 If this goes on month after month after month, then she's gonna have to make a decision with her family and her friends about what her future holds. Because this isn't just about California. It's also about the nation. And we just can't, with this one-vote margin, and expect every other person to be there every single time.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Some, some of your...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 It's gonna become an issue as the months go by. But I'm taking her at her word that she's gonna return.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWEET FROM REP. RO KHANNA\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) 'Cause, 'cause some of your Democratic colleagues, in the House anyway are, are saying she should resign now. Let's look at Ro Khanna had to say. He tweeted, "It's time for Senator Feinstein to resign. We need to put the country ahead of personal loyalty. While she has had a lifetime of public service, it is obvious she can no longer fulfill her duties. Not speaking out undermines our credibility as elected representatives of the people." What do you say to Ro Khanna?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 What I say is this, one, she's gotten off the committee, and that is, or will get off the committee. That is the most important thing to happen right now. Secondly, I think when you look at the history, people have returned to the Senate when they're sick. She said she has shingles. She has had shingles. And so, months down the road here, I think you get to that moment of that decision point. But, right now she says she's gonna return. Let's make sure that happens. And it sure better happen before the debt ceiling vote.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: EXCLUSIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARYLAND GOV. WES MOORE DISCUSSES HIS STATE'S PLAN AS THE FIGHT OVER THE ABORTION PILL HEADS TO THE SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and before you go, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , we've now had, you know, two sets of, of revelations from \uc2 Pro Publica\uc2 . One about the vacations he took with, with Harlan Crow, who he described as a family friend. And now turns out Harlan Crow bought his mother's house, which he was a, a part owner of. How serious is this?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RPT: JUSTICE THOMAS DID NOT DISCLOSE DEAL WITH BILLIONAIRE\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 Serious. When you have billionaires who are on boards with cases pending before the Court, buying a justice's mom's home and renovating it and then that justice doesn't report it. This isn't even an exception for personal friendships, Jonathan.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 This is a case where the law clearly says you have to report these things. Yet he reported that same year a medallion he was given from Yale. Another year he reported when he was given tires. But he doesn't report this? And he didn't report the lavish vacations on yachts? It is time for ethics rules in the Supreme Court that are clear and enforceable. I said this last time I was on with you on this very show, when he wasn't recusing himself from cases pending before the court regarding the insurrection, given his wife's, what we know now about her emails and texts and the like.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 This should not be a double standard. Every federal judge in the country comes under these ethics rules. So, if they don't do it then the Congress should do it. And that's why we are having a hearing to cover this on the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Senator Klobuchar, thank you for being here. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM-MN) (JUDICIARY COMMITTEE)\par \par \uc2 It was great to be on, Jonathan. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you. Coming up, we'll be joined by one of the Democratic Party's fastest rising stars, Maryland Governor Wes Moore. Plus, our Roundtable tracks growing 2024 presidential field. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABCTHISWEEK\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230421ej4g00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS SUNDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY SWEET 16 SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight a sweet 16 party turns deadly after gunfire erupts injuring multiple victims, many of them teens. At least four people are dead in Alabama, including a rising football star. What we're learning about the victims and the investigation. President Biden calls for action as mass shootings hit record levels with more than 160 already this year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT FROM LEAKED SECRETS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also tonight, new fallout from the leak of top secret intelligence including a call for some to be fired, while the Secretary of State tries to reassure allies. Plus why drumming up support for Ukraine is becoming a tough sell.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOZENS KILLED IN BATTLE FOR SUDAN\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Dozens killed in the battle for Sudan. The struggle between two rival military factions, the violence is apparent in satellite images. Tonight we hear from an American traveling in Sudan. She tells us about the nonstop fighting. Tonight, the new efforts to reach a truce.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TERMINAL EVACUATED\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking news out of Nashville, a terminal evacuated after noxious fumes filled the air, what authorities are now saying.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEATHER WHIPLASH\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Weather whiplash. Just days after temperatures topped 80 degrees, a massive spring storm system set to dump heavy snow across the upper Midwest before it heads to the northeast. Ron Marciano times it all out.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR ABORTION PILL DECISION LOOMS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tensions rise as the Supreme Court considers limits on an abortion pill, that decision could be just days away. Abortion rights activists are asking if birth control could be targeted next.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THREE AMERICANS MISSING AT SEA\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The urgent search for three Americans missing at sea. They were headed from Mexico to San Diego when they simply vanished. The nerve-racking wait for family members who say they're experienced boaters.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2 : GUARDSMAN SOUGHT HIT MAN JOB\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 An air national guard member arrested. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  says that he wanted to become a hit man, even a applying on line and bragging about his military experience. How agents tracked him down.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOSTON STRONG\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And Boston strong. A survivor of the marathon bombing is now paying it forward, turning her personal horror into hope.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight"\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020230418ej4g00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR ABORTION PILL DECISION LOOMS WEEKEND PROTESTS AHEAD OF SUPREME COURT RULING\b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY SWEET 16 SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, DEAD, INJURED, PARTY, TAYLOR, FLOYD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY SWEET 16 SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, DOCUMENTS, FALLOUT, TEIXEIRA, TURNER, BLINKEN, ALLIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT FROM LEAKED SECRETS\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, FIGHTING, CONFLICT, KILLED, INJURED, PARTHASARATHY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOZENS KILLED IN BATTLE FOR SUDAN\par \par \uc2 NASHVILLE, TERMINAL, EVACUATED, ODOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TERMINAL EVACUATED\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, HAIL, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLAST OF SPRING SNOW\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SUPREME COURT, PROTESTS, \uc2 FDA\uc2 , KLOBUCHAR, CASSIDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR ABORTION PILL DECISION LOOMS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rob, thank you. Back here at home, the battle over the abortion pill is intensifying. Protests this weekend as the Supreme Court considers whether to grant the Biden administration's request to preserve the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's decades old approval of the drug used in the majority of abortions in this country. A ruling is expected in the next few days. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze reports in from the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR ABORTION PILL DECISION LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEEKEND PROTESTS AHEAD OF SUPREME COURT RULING\par \par \uc2 PROTESTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Are we going to back down?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight the fight over abortion reaching a fever pitch.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is freedom.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As the Supreme Court, less than a year after it overturned Roe versus Wade, prepares to weigh in this week on a consequential abortion pill case. Protests this weekend from LA to Washington.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Honestly I don't have a lot of faith in the Supreme Court right now.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We're here to counter them and celebrate the abortion pill is becoming more regulated.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) By 11:59 PM Wednesday the nation's highest court, with its conservative majority, is expected to decide if the abortion pill, Mifepristone, used in more than half of US abortions, should stay available in states where it's legal. A ruling this month by a federal judge in Texas tried to suspend \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of the medication, which would ban it nationwide.\par \par \uc2 SEN AMY KLOBUCHAR (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 What is it going to be next? Is that judge going to not let birth control pills, are we going to have a judge that doesn't like Lipitor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR ABORTION PILL DECISION LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRITICS: COULD CREATE "SLIPPERY SLOPE" FOR \uc2 FDA\uc2  APPROVALS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But some Republicans are downplaying critics concerns that the Texas decision could undermine the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's ability to approve other drugs.\par \par \uc2 SEN BILL CASSIDY (REP) (LOUISIANA)\par \par \uc2 I think that's totally alarmist. It's totally alarmist. And, by the way, when did the \uc2 FDA\uc2  go above the law.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A recent \uc2 PEW\uc2  poll found 53% of Americans say abortion via medication should be legal in their state. 22% say it should be illegal. Providers like Dr. Kristin Brandy in limbo as they await the high court's decision.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is a medication I literally give every single day of my practice. Losing this medication will be devastating.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Elizabeth Schulze joins us now from the Supreme Court. Elizabeth, critics of the Texas judge's ruling argue that it could create a slippery slope for \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of other drugs if upheld. How might that argument play with the Supreme Court?\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Linsey, the former \uc2 FDA\uc2  Commissioner who oversaw the approval of Mifepristone more than 20 years ago, tells us tonight it's disturbing that the Texas ruling could undermine public confidence in the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval process, which is seen as the gold standard to determine if drugs are safe. The justices haven't yet indicated how they'd lean on this decision. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020230418ej4g00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 COFFEE TOK TIKTOK TREND HAS USERS PUTTING LEMON IN COFFEE\b0\par\par\uc2 806 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH, CHEROT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES AS MORTALITIES RISE\par \par \uc2 AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT, TRICHTER, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, SLEEP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 "ON BRAND", LICHT\par \par \uc2 "THE SOULMATE", HEPWORTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 CHERRY BLOSSOM, FESTIVAL, WALTER\par \par \uc2 FELLER, LEMON, COFFEE, WEIGHT LOSS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COFFEE TOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIKTOK TREND HAS USERS PUTTING LEMON IN COFFEE - BUT DOES IT HELP LOSE WEIGHT?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "GMA." And the coffee trend that's feeling your feed, TikTok users adding lemon to their morning joe, saying it helps lose weight. But is this a coffee cure or is it sour? Here to myth bust is our got to registered dietitian and nutritionist Maya Feller. Maya, good morning to you. We've got to put this all together. They're talking about lemon and coffee, I feel like I need to brush my teeth with Sensodyne just talking about it. But the weight loss benefits, is it really there?\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN / NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my goodness, Whit. Listen, further research is needed to actually definitively say that putting lemon in your coffee will help you lose weight or do anything for cardiovascular disease or your diabetes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NO STUDIES SHOW THEY CAUSE WEIGHT LOSS WHEN COMBINED\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN / NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 What researchers are saying is that, listen, these are observational studies. Maybe there are other compounds that are at play.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Yeah, that's right. And this is really becoming the latest trend on the internet, so it is concerning to you as a nutritionist that you are seeing this play out on the internet, on TikTok, going viral.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN / NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 I am so frustrated by this. For people who want to engage in mindful and intentional weight loss, I say do not do these extreme diets, this is a hard no.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, okay, so I feel like we know the answer. But in your expert opinion, what about just in general getting health info from social media?\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN / NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 No, absolutely not. Seek out a qualified health care provider. A physician. A dietitian.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE SIZE DOES NOT FIT ALL, TALK TO A HEALTHCARE PROFESSIONAL TO DETERMINE BEST DIET FOR YOU\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN / NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Remember, we all have different nutritional needs. One size does not work for all. What works for your auntie, your uncle, your neighbor might not be right for you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, there's one social media, Maya Feller.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, yeah. yeah.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's where they need to go for nutritional advice.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN / NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Exactly, 100%\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, so my morning coffee is still very important to me. But what beverages should we be drinking in the morning?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COFFEE, TEA, WATER\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN / NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 So, if you like tea and you if you like coffee, absolutely go ahead and enjoy them. I also say that hydration is really important. You can get some of your hydration from fruits, from vegetables, herbal teas, sparkling water, still water. You really just want to make sure you are well hydrated.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, great. Always appreciated, Maya. Thank you so much. And we'll be right back after this.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right, you just saw it right there, get more "GMA" in your day with "GMA Life" streaming on ABC News Live his morning at 9:00 and 11:00 AM and 1:00 PM Eastern. Find ABC News Live on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 , the ABC News app, and on abcnews.com.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All the places.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All the places.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. And we'll see you right back here tomorrow morning. Have a great weekend, everybody.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) See you, everybody.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f0006c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS MIDNIGHT MUST-HAVES\b0\par\par\uc2 1,450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \