w, a couple minutes to install. Anybody could do it. Works best in a metal-framed be bed. So, you can turn that kind of boring metal frame into a fabulous looking modern sleek, almost like your hotel bed, but in your bedroom. We've got a variety of sizes, colors. These are really great, $65 and free shipping, too.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $65-$85 +FREE SHIPPING FOR GMA, 50%\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it hides all the junk that you're trying to, like, hide under the bed.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, exactly. Tory, thank you so much. We appreciate it. Of course, we partnered with all these companies.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's the pro tip.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, exactly, each deal at good morningamerica.com. And coming up, the National Cherry Blossom Festival Parade. Ike Ejiochi is out there with some friendly faces. Yes, the grand marshal...\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f00067\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES\b0\par\par\uc2 1,233 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH, CHEROT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES AS MORTALITIES RISE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back. Now to our "GMA Cover Story" and Black Maternal Health Week started by the Black Mamas Matter Alliance to raise awareness around the inequities black mothers face nationwide. And joining me now is Dr. Elizabeth Cherot, a practicing OB/GYN, is also senior vice president and chief medical and health officer for the March of Dimes. Good morning, and thank you for being with us. She said she'd rather be delivering a baby in the hallway than on TV right now. Several studies show that maternal mortality and severe maternal morbidity among women in this country is going in the wrong direction. The surgeon general, I talked to him last week, he said that c-section rates are a concerned. And even the New York State Birth Equity Project has announced new initiatives to try to bring down the c-section rate 5%. Talk to me about the concern there.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 So, first, thank you. Thank you for highlighting Black Maternal Health Week longer and really important to be talking about experiences of black women versus experiences of white women. And if we aren't doing that, we're not really talking about women's health, so really appreciate being here. And the statistics are all going in the wrong direction. We've got mortality rates are up 89%. We've got preterm birth up by 4%. And, yes, c-section rates all going the wrong direction. Despite really doing big efforts, we are seeing big disparities when it comes to black and brown women in this country.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And when we talk about those disparities for back and brown women, what is at the heart of it?\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 It's a really complex problem, but it's really, and is fundamental, there's racism. There's bias. There are structural social issues we need to address. And one of biggest ones the March of Dimes is addressing is about access to care.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REASONS FOR GROWING DISPARITIES\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 We know access to care is one of the biggest barriers to healthy moms, healthy babies and families. And so, when we think about access to care, I think about just getting in for that prenatal visit.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 And if you don't have insurance or you don't have access, a maternity care desert is someplace where there is no OB provider, there's no hospital or birth center to deliver in. And we are seeing a rise in those across the country. And I bet you're thinking that's all rural.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 It's actually urban.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's actually 30% to 50% of counties, right?\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 There you go, Janai. Exactly. And so, how do we solve for that? I would say, at March of Dimes, we're here talking about it. We're here educating. We're trying to do a lot of implicit bias training for provider fours. We're trying to get to women and get them educated. We're also really trying to advocate and do research. And we're doing, we actually have a health equity center at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2 . It's our inaugural center for health equity and really trying to look at doulas and other outcomes and innovations. Elizabeth Howell, fantastic OB/GYN chairman there, really pushing this that we support. And then we do a ton of advocacy. We know that postpartum period is really something that we, as woman six weeks later, you're not done.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Right.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 It's not wrapped up in a bow and we are not on TV. What we are really trying to do is advocate to extend postpartum care for a full year because we know mental health, we know that cardiovascular doesn't end after six weeks, neither does diabetes. And so, all those conditions need to be looked at.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it's in that period, that we're seeing most maternal deaths happen, a week to a year after a woman gets birth.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I want to bring up this graphic that the \uc2 New York State Department of Health\uc2  actually just recently came out with these lists of patients' rights and things that they're going to try to do better.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And number 11 on the list is making sure that patients go home with postpartum education and knowing the warning signs. How crucial is that for the health of a mom and her baby?\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 It's incredibly, incredibly crucial. These are times when you can still seize afterbirth. There's having complications, readmission for your hypertension, the most common times is within those first 16 days. But then you need to be continued to be monitored and followed.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 And it does, like I said, it doesn't end at 42 days, it doesn't end six weeks. It really needs to be long-term, which is why we're really trying to extend the Momnibus Act. And Medicaid is different depending on the geography you're in.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 And where you live matters. And it shouldn't. And we really believe at the March of Dimes that it doesn't matter about race, geography or wealth, we should have better outcomes for all our moms and babies.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the fact that most moms are seeing a doctor for the first time until about four to six weeks after, another issue.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That we'll have to talk more about. Thank you so much for being here with us.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH CHEROT (MARCH OF DIMES)\par \par \uc2 Thanks for having me. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, over to you.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Important conversation. Janai, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f00064\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALIZA LICHT IS "ON BRAND" "SHAPE YOUR NARRATIVE, SHARE YOUR VISION & SHIFT THEIR PERCEPTION"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,222 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH, CHEROT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES AS MORTALITIES RISE\par \par \uc2 AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT, TRICHTER, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, SLEEP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 "ON BRAND", LICHT\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, now to leveling up your life and whether you are looking for new job or just want to grow yourself personally, establishing a brand for yourself, can make a big difference. And joining us now is personal branding expert Aliza Licht, who is also the author of the book, "On Brand." Perfectly titled. So, what are how, thank you so much for being here with us. When people hear brands, they may initially think I'm not an influencer, I don't want to be famous, why do I need branding?\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 Well, first of all, thank you for having me here. So, everyone has some version of a personal brand. It starts with what makes you, you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALIZA LICHT IS "ON BRAND"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOT TO "SHAPE YOUR NARRATIVE, SHARE YOUR VISION & SHIFT THEIR PERCEPTION"\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 So, whether you're trying to get promoted or, you're trying to pivot industries, you're an entrepreneur pitching investors, it doesn't matter. Every single person needs to understand how they're showing up, no matter what the medium.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, where do people start?\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 Well, they start with first understanding what do they want to be known for. That self-reflection is really important, because everything needs to be geared towards that north star.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO BUILD YOUR BRAND\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 And how you see yourself needs to match how people see you. So, you've got to ask your network, you've got to ask around and say, hey, what are three adjectives you would ask me, you would describe me at work? And do they match how you think about yourself?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, man, that's a little scary.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I don't what to say.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll do that after the show, after the show.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What does that say about my brand?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Where do I begin?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, exactly, right? All right, there are a lot of college graduates who are entering the workforce now. What is the number one piece of advice that you would give them to get started?\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 I think that college doesn't teach you how important your network is. And not just collecting business cards, but building authentic relationships that you'd keep in touch with and grow with, the people that you are meeting. And every person you meet can be someone along the way that can help you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRANDING TIP: ADVICE FOR NEW GRADS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUILDING YOUR NETWORK IS CRUCIAL\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 And I think people, especially when you have internships they usually do their intentions and they move on and they forget about those people because they're moving onto the next. But let's build those relationships.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think that's so interesting because the idea of networking has always been really intimidating to me. But building real relationships feels much more natural, so it's nice to hear you say that. What about people who are looking to further their careers, whether they are unemployed right now or looking to pivot, who may be dealing with imposter syndrome.\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 I love this question? So, I believe that if you're in the room, you belong there. And a lot of people, when they get in the room, they question it. They're like, "Well, am I deserving? Am I smart enough? And I really the person who should be here?"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRANDING TIP: FIGHTING IMPOSTER SYNDROME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IF YOU'RE IN THE ROOM, YOU BELONG THERE\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 But what they should be thinking is, what can I do know that I am here? What impression can I be making?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I love that. And you say it's really important to celebrate your win, but you say it is important to do it elegantly. What do you mean by that?\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 Well, this book is meant to shine a spotlight on yourself and for people to become their own heroes, but not to the extent that they become a villain. I'm not trying to create monsters here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRANDING TIP: KEEP TRACK OF YOUR WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHARE WINS ELEGANTLY, PROMOTE OTHERS TOO\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 So, when I say share your wins strategically, the truth is that if you're waiting around for people to notice that you're good at something, that's not a strategy. So, if you share your wins strategically and elegantly and you amplify five other people for every one time you're talking about yourself, I think the world will be a better place.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's good.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, key information. So, also, one thing that I thought that you say that's interesting, especially in 2023, is that people don't actually need to use social media to be able to do this effectively, right?\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 This is a really important principle in "On Brand" because I didn't want to exclude people who were, that's not for me. I mean, personally, I believe every personal person should be on \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 . But how you show up in real life is just as important.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRANDING TIP: SOCIAL MEDIA NOT REQUIRED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUILDING AUTHENTIC RELATIONSHIPS IN REAL LIFE IS JUST AS IMPORTANT\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 What you choose to align with, your attitude, your mannerisms, earning social capital, building relationships, that also establishes your personal brand.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Important tips to remind not only just us here but everyone watching. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 ALIZA LICHT (AUTHOR "ON BRAND")\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And your book "On Brand" is out Tuesday, April 18th, so check it out. And we will be right back here on weekend "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f00068\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GMA BUZZ PICK "THE SOULMATE"\b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH, CHEROT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES AS MORTALITIES RISE\par \par \uc2 AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT, TRICHTER, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, SLEEP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 "ON BRAND", LICHT\par \par \uc2 "THE SOULMATE", HEPWORTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now to this Saturday's "GMA Buzz Pick." "The Soulmate" by Saly Hepworth, it's one of the most anticipated thrillers of 2023. And here's Sally to tell us all about it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THE SOULMATE" SALLY HEPWORTH\par \par \uc2 SALLY HEPWORTH (AUTHOR "THE SOULMATE")\par \par \uc2 Hi, "GMA," I'm Sally Hepworth. In my book, "The Soulmate," married couple Gabe and Pippa moved in to a beautiful Seaside cottage on a tall cliff where they discovered, to their horror, people go to end their lives. Gabe makes it his mission to stop people from jumping, literally talking them off the ledge. Until one night, he isn't successful. His wife Pippa was watching through the window the night the woman jumped and she noticed Gabe was acting strangely. Late, when she discovers that Gabe knew the woman, secrets and lies start tumbling out.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ooh.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Having secrets and lies. I'm in for that. "The Soulmate" is available now. And keep reading along with us on our \uc2 Instagram\uc2  @GMABookClub. Gio?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we will read.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f00069\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NATIONAL CHERRY BLOSSOM FESTIVAL PARADE DC IS IN FULL BLOOM AS SPRINGTIME EVENT RETURNS TO CONSTITUTION AVENUE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,402 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH, CHEROT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES AS MORTALITIES RISE\par \par \uc2 AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT, TRICHTER, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, SLEEP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 "ON BRAND", LICHT\par \par \uc2 "THE SOULMATE", HEPWORTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 CHERRY BLOSSOM, FESTIVAL, WALTER\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And spring is in bloom. The National Cherry Blossom Festival Parade marching down Constitution Avenue this morning. And look who's there, our Ike Ejiochi right there in DC. Look, looking, look at the pink tie and everything. You got it going on. Hey, Ike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL CHERRY BLOSSOM FESTIVAL PARADE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DC IS IN FULL BLOOM AS SPRINGTIME EVENT RETURNS TO CONSTITUTION AVENUE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've got the vest. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're never going to see me dressed this nicely ever again, I'm just letting you know right now. But I got to get festive. You know why? Because this is the most exciting time of year right here in Washington, DC. And it's the National Cherry Blossom Springtime Parade, and it starts just in a couple of hours ago. But listen, this had been going on here in Washington, DC for quite some time now.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It actually started back in 1912 when the then mayor of Tokyo gifted Japanese cherry blossoms to the city of Washington, DC. Ever since then, every year, the city had been celebrating that gift with a three-week-long event, obviously starting with the peak bloom of the cherry blossoms and ending right here at this parade. Now, today, obviously I said it starts in a couple of hours, but there's been people from all over the city, from all over the world, almost 700,000 people come here to see this parade and the other festivities.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They look for high school marching bands from all over the country, floats, there's a whole bunch of DC singers here. So, you know that (inaudible) is going to get hopping is just a little bit. And I said, 700,000 people come here. One very special person is here with me now.\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Hi.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LISA ANN WALTER IN BLOOM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "ABBOTT ELEMENTARY" STAR KICKS OFF NATIONAL CHERRY BLOSSOM FESTIVAL\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hello. it's Lisa Ann Walter. We know her from "Abbott Elementary," "The Parent Trap," everything. But of course, you're a DC native. Welcome.\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 I am originally from the DMV and I'm so happy be back home.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, like you said, DMV, all right, Silver Springs, right?\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How does it feel to be taking part of this cherry blossom festival you've known for so long?\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Well, not only knew it. But when out to high school in Silver Spring, our Blair Blazers marched. I was a palm. So, I have been down this parade doing poms. I didn't bring poms today. But I bet you I can find some.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, we can find you some real quick.\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, there they are. Look.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You have any poms you want to borrow real quick?\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 But I'm just thrilled to be back home. We went to the Smithsonian yesterday, trying to get some crabs but they are not really in season quite yet. We're still waiting on that. I might go duck pin bowling later.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Duck pin bowling?\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah. That's all stuff you've got to do.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A little race with the (inaudible) president? That's a good one, too. Right?\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, sure. Why not?\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, why not. Is there any like fun memory that you remember from those parades back in the day?\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Oh, my gosh, yeah. I mean, first of all, it's all the people coming out. You've got women in traditional Japanese gowns on floats over here. You've got all the flowers are even though we missed the blooms a little bit this year, you've got all these beautiful cherry blossoms on the float. It's just, it's a gorgeous spectacle and all the people that come out to see it. I like the little guys with giant hats on the little bikes? That's my favorite. They're ridiculous, but fantastic.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I love it too.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, at this point, you're on "GMA" and "GMA3" this week so it's good to see you, my friend. What's a must to thing for you there when you're home in DC?\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Well, some of the stuff that I mentioned because when they try to give you crabcakes back where I live now, in LA, they've got like green peppers in it. I'm like, what are you doing? It's crab and mayonnaise, maybe some Old Bay, that's it. Stop there.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There you go.\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 So, and some of the clubs that I used to dance when I was here. I went to a catholic university here in DC and we used to go down to the 930 Club and get our punk rock dance on.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible)\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Oh, yeah, this is the town, listen, this is the town where I learned how to the hustle.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The hustle?\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 At a club (inaudible) called Dimples. My mother would bring me and I will just get, do the hustle. In DC is where we started the hustle. And then you turn me.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, oh, oh, oh.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do the hustle.\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 But I was 13 and she used to take me out and let me dance. We were nuts. I don't know what we are thinking, but we had a good time.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But in the clip for the next episode of "Abbott Elementary" I saw you ragging on DC a little bit.\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 ...an entertainment exhibit, democracy in America, it's great stuff happening here. If you haven't visited, a lot of it, you know what it is, it's free. Your tax dollars pay for it.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 LISA ANN WALTER ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 Come down here. Go check out the free stuff.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There you go. The DC tourism board is going to thank you. Lisa Ann Walter...\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If it's free, it's for me.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I've lost you. We lost you. We got too happy.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's okay.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're having a blast out there. We appreciate having you both. Ike, too.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) hustle. We're going to have some fun. It's going to be great.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f0006a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH, CHEROT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES AS MORTALITIES RISE\par \par \uc2 AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT, TRICHTER, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, SLEEP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 "ON BRAND", LICHT\par \par \uc2 "THE SOULMATE", HEPWORTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 CHERRY BLOSSOM, FESTIVAL, WALTER\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we are going to go back over to Somara for a check of the weather.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, well, they say April showers bring May flowers. But all the rain we saw in California that led to an early super bloom out in Diamond Valley Lake, take a look.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is the biggest one since 2019. And you know what? You can see this from space. So, aliens, go there first when you land. All right, so here's a look at New York. So, we we're going from the West Coast to the East Coast, beautiful sunrise. New York had its hottest April day in New York City since 2012, yesterday we hit 90 degrees.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLLEN FORECAST\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, everyone is going to be experiencing the high pollen that we have from Phoenix to Oklahoma City. Very high in the southeast mainly tree pollen, up into the northeast high pollen as well. A little bit modern as you head to areas like the Pacific Northwest. That's a look at the weather across the country, let's see what's going on in your neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...full effect. Yesterday, I was able to get outside. I did some walking around the park. Did you all enjoy your time in the heat?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm. Yes.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we're cooling back down.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We've got all the sun when we could. But spring has sprung, so we we'll take it.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Somara. And still coming up, it is the sour trend taking over TikTok, just the latest trend. Does adding lemon to your morning cup of coffee help you lose weight? Our dear friend Maya Feller is standing by to break it all down. Come back. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f0006b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 KIDS ON AUTISM SPECTRUM SHARE THEIR VOICES RECORDING TRANSIT ANNOUNCEMENTS FOR AUTISM ACCEPTANCE MONTH\b0\par\par\uc2 854 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH, CHEROT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES AS MORTALITIES RISE\par \par \uc2 AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT, TRICHTER, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to a project that happening in major cities across the country this Autism Acceptance Month. And ABC's Will Ganss met some kids who are doing their part. Will, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS ON AUTISM SPECTRUM SHARE THEIR VOICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORDING TRANSIT ANNOUNCEMENTS FOR AUTISM ACCEPTANCE MONTH\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. Good morning, Gio. From San Francisco to Washington, DC, Atlanta to Newark, all aboard for the Autism Transit Project. And mind the gap, because this train of inspiration is leaving the station.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For millions of Americans, that morning commute is about to level up.\par \par \uc2 IMMANUEL (ATLANTA GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 Hi, my name is Immanuel and I really like trains. Please help us to keep the train clean. Please, don't litter.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This month, the Autism Transit Project giving the voice, literally, to kids on the autism spectrum.\par \par \uc2 GOYO (SAN FRANCISCO CALIFORNIA)\par \par \uc2 BART\uc2 . Please stay away from the yellow lines on the edge of the platform. It makes the conductor nervous when you get too near, and it is unsafe.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, a star is born.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Making those public transit announcements in major cities all over the country.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN TRICHTER (AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT / CO-FOUNDER HUBBARD DAY)\par \par \uc2 What we've learned about this community, these people, is that they often have a tendency to perseverate or focus very hard on things that atypical people find interesting.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Goyo will be the voice of the \uc2 BART\uc2  trains in his Bay Area hometown.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Goyo, what does autism means to you?\par \par \uc2 GOYO (SAN FRANCISCO CALIFORNIA)\par \par \uc2 Oh, well, a difference in your brain, in the way you think, act, and just the way you do stuff. It's a difference not a disability.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Advantages like knowing how to rick roll an interview.\par \par \uc2 GOYO (SAN FRANCISCO CALIFORNIA)\par \par \uc2 You know the rules and so do I.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Unfortunately, no Rick Astley karaoke in the \uc2 BART\uc2  trains in San Fran. But down in Atlanta, Immanuel is ready for his big moment.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How do you stay so positive and so warm all the time?\par \par \uc2 IMMANUEL (ATLANTA GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 I really don't know, it's just me thing I guess.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in the Washington, DC metro area, Ezra is stepping into the spotlight.\par \par \uc2 EZRA (WASHINGTON DC)\par \par \uc2 I'm kind of nervous because everyone was wanting to know about me.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ezra and his parents thrilled to help raise awareness for families touched with autism.\par \par \uc2 NICK RODRIGUEZ (FATHER OF EZRA)\par \par \uc2 One thing I've learned from being Ezra's dad is that neurodiversity is another important kind of diversity.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 NICK RODRIGUEZ (FATHER OF EZRA)\par \par \uc2 And that it needs the same kind of energy and effort and work from all of us.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Which is exactly what the Autism Transit Project aims to do.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN TRICHTER (AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT / CO-FOUNDER HUBBARD DAY)\par \par \uc2 The project will therefore show these children to a broader swath of the public. Different but similar, and no less than beautiful.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The latest stats from the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  reminding us that one in 100 children on the autism spectrum. And as we've learned from those families, it really is a spectrum of needs, abilities, and interests. This month it's not just about awareness and acceptance, but about celebrating that neurodiversity, you guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that moment with a little boy, how do you stay so positive? "It's a me thing."\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's a me thing. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'll take a bit of his me thing and try to incorporate into my day-to-day.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We all learn something from them. Will, thank you so much. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f00065\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH, CHEROT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK SPOTLIGHTS RACIAL INEQUITIES AS MORTALITIES RISE\par \par \uc2 AUTISM TRANSIT PROJECT, TRICHTER, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's turn it over to Somara for another check of the weather. Somara, good morning.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning. All right, so we're talking wildfires. And normally you think, West Coast.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is a Manchester Township, New Jersey. If you missed it, dynamic video coming out from this week with wildfires burning thousands of acres there. This was just yesterday in Rockland County, New York. Believe it or not, this started by sparks on a train. So, what do you need for wildfires? We need gusty winds and dry conditions, real hot conditions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HEAT\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have record heat yesterday. Hartford, Connecticut, 96. Concord, New Hampshire breaking a 153-year record for that day, coming in at 90 degrees, even pretty hot in Boston.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO SPRING\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As far as the heat, it's moving out, we're going to cool things down. So, if you prefer temperatures in the 60s, hang tight in the East Coast. Today, Saturday, Boston 64, even down to DC by Monday, 68. That's a look at the weather across the country, let's see what's going on in your neighborhood\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f00066\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 789 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, DALVEN, BAPTIST, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, now to the ongoing battle over the abortion pill, mifepristone. The Supreme Court weighing in overnight, allowing access for now, ABC is Mireya Villarreal has been following those developments. Good morning again to you, Mireya.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning. You know, the Supreme Court is going to take about the next five days or so to review everything that has happened so far, but we've spoken with a lot of clinics. They say the uncertainty of all of this is really creating a lot of confusion with the women who need these abortion rights or abortion services and the medical staff trying to help them.\par \par \uc2 DEMONSTRATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We need change, and we need it now.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Emotions running high this morning.\par \par \uc2 DEMONSTRATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And bring signs, bring banners, bring yourself back here.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As the fierce debate over the future of abortion plays out nationwide, the Supreme Court stepping in.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT ISSUES STAY OF ABORTION PILL RULING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE DECISION TEMPORARILY KEEPS MIFEPRISTONE WIDELY AVAILABLE FOR NOW\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  issuing an administrative stay of the ruling in Texas that would overturn the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's original approval of the abortion medication mifepristone that would essentially take the pill off the market, now giving the court until April 20th to review the case before deciding what their next steps will be.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER DALVEN (DIRECTOR \uc2 ACLU\uc2  REPRODUCTIVE FREEDOM PROJECT)\par \par \uc2 It's good news for the patients that are going to be seen tomorrow, but it is far from over.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The last-minute weigh-in from the nation's highest court bringing a temporary sigh of relief for abortion rights advocates after conflicting rulings in Washington state and Texas have left the use of the drug nationwide up in the air.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER DALVEN (DIRECTOR \uc2 ACLU\uc2  REPRODUCTIVE FREEDOM PROJECT)\par \par \uc2 We were talking to doctors around the country and there was just mass confusion and chaos.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Attorney Erik Baptist with the anti-abortion rights group \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  represents four doctors and four medical associations from the original Texas case.\par \par \uc2 ERIK BAPTIST (SENIOR COUNSEL ALLIANCE DEFENDING FREEDOM)\par \par \uc2 And we're confident again that when the courts, any court, looks at the fact, the facts and the law of this case, they're going to agree with us. So, this is just the next step in a long lengthy litigation.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we have spoken with clinics that are providing abortion services in states that still allow this. They tell us right now they can see patients within one to two weeks, but they are very concerned. If mifepristone comes off the market that that will create a lot of confusion, a lot of frustration and maybe even an increase in the abortion services where surgery is needed and requested. So, again, very much a wait-and-see situation but still very concerning for women across this country. Guys?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. Mireya, thank you for that update.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 3 MINUTES, BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Still coming up here in our "Morning Menu," sounding the alarm on rising maternal mortality in this country, why women of color are especially at risk.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 7 MINUTES, AUTISM ACCEPTANCE MONTH\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also ahead this morning on "GMA," we're all aboard for a story from Will Ganz.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right public transit systems across the country are giving kids on the spectrum of voice this Autism Acceptance Month. We'll show you how.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 11 MINUTES, MIDNIGHT MUST-HAVES!\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, Tory Johnson is in the house with midnight must-haves. Don't sleep on these savings. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f00063\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 09:00 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, CAMPAIGN, PRIME MINISTER\par \par \uc2 MONTANA, TIKTOK, BAN, REGIER, SULLIVAN, HASKINS\par \par \uc2 CASH APP, LEE, SUSPECT, ARRESTED, STABBING, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 POLICE, NEW MEXICO, FATALITY, HEBBE, DOTSON\par \par \uc2 OREGON, MONEY, WINDOW, INTERSTATE FIVE\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, TEXTS, TRIAL, EX-HUSBAND, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 BEARS, HIBERNATION, SNOWPACK, FOOD, HASCH\par \par \uc2 AAA, HYUNDAI, TIKTOK, CHALLENGE, TARGETED, SHIELDS\par \par \uc2 MCNUTT, \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , NBA, PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's our second hour.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED LEAKER IN COURT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Overnight, new details in that major national security leak. The 21-year-old suspect appearing in court. What we're learning about the charges and how prosecutor say the damaging documents ended up online.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT STEPPING IN\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court stepping in on the abortion pill battle, blocking the Texas judge's ban, allowing access for at least a few more days.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK" SPOTLIGHTS INEQUITIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HEALTH CARE IS FAILING BLACK MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, this morning, how the health care system is failing black mothers? Why women of color are especially at risk as maternal mortality rise. And what's being done to address rampant racial inequities?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEVELING UP YOUR PROFESSIONAL & PERSONAL LIFE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALIZA LICHT IS "ON BRAND"\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Aliza Licht is "On Brand." The best-selling author joins us live, turning the page on her new book all about leveling up your professional and personal life.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEMON TREND HAS TIKTOK JUMPING FOR JAVA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COFFEE TOK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And coffee tok. Taking on the trend that TikTok jumping for java, putting lemon in their morning cup of Joe.\par \par \uc2 VOICEOVER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Squeeze half a lemon or lime.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But does sour sip help lose weight? As we say, good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 It's Saturday morning, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How good is that song?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So good. So good. I can buy myself flowers. Good morning, America. Good Saturday morning. Glad to have you with us. Spring is in bloom this morning. And Ike Ejiochi is at the National Cherry Blossom Festival Parade in Washington, DC, look at that, where "Abbott Elementary" star Lisa Ann Walter is an honorary parade marshal. She will join us live coming up in our second hour. Maybe we'll get Ike to play the saxophone.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Maybe. We've been working on this for a long time.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We'll see if today's the day. Looking forward to that. We do have a lot to cover this morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f00061\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPREME COURT WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION PILL WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION MEANS FOR ABORTION ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,215 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK: FACING A JUDGE\par \par \uc2 LEAKER, PENTAGON, PRISON, TEIXEIRA, ARRESTED, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 DISCORD, LEAKED, TEIXEIRA, CHINESE, SPY\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, DALVEN, BAPTIST, EDELMAN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the battle over the abortion pill, Mifepristone. The Supreme Court weighing in, allowing access for now and avoiding major changes that were set to take effect overnight. ABC's Mireya Villarreal has the latest developments. Mireya, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Whit. Yeah, this morning, abortion rights advocates are actually breathing a sigh of relief, but they realize, they tell me this is not a win, this is a temporary pause on the case and they realize the clock is still ticking on Mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We need change and we need it now.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Emotions running high this morning...\par \par \uc2 ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And bring signs, bring banners, bring yourself back here.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...as the fierce debate over the future of abortion plays out nationwide, the Supreme Court stepping in. Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  issuing an administrative stay of the ruling in Texas that would overturn the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's original approval of the abortion medication, Mifepristone that would essentially take the pill off the market.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT ISSUES STAY OF ABORTION PILL RULING. THE DECISION TEMPORARILY KEEPS MIFEPRISTONE WIDELY AVAILABLE FOR NOW\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now giving the court until April 20th to review the case before deciding that their next steps will be. In a statement, the White House saying the stakes "could not be higher." and that "For now, Mifepristone remains available and approved for safe and effective use."\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER DALVEN (DIRECTOR \uc2 ACLU\uc2  REPRODUCTIVE FREEDOM PROJECT)\par \par \uc2 It's good news for the patients that are going to be seen tomorrow, but it is far from over.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The last-minute weigh-in from the nation's highest court bringing a temporary sigh of relief for abortion rights advocates after conflicting rulings in Washington State and Texas have left the use of the drug nationwide up in the air.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER DALVEN (DIRECTOR \uc2 ACLU\uc2  REPRODUCTIVE FREEDOM PROJECT)\par \par \uc2 We were talking to doctors around the country and there was just mass confusion and chaos.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Attorney Erik Baptist with the anti-abortion rights group \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  represents four doctors and four medical associations from the original Texas case.\par \par \uc2 ERIK BAPTIST (SENIOR COUNSEL ALLIANCE DEFENDING FREEDOM)\par \par \uc2 And we are confident again that when the courts, any court, looks at the facts and the law of this case, they're going to agree with us. So, this is just the next step in a long, lengthy litigation.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The uncertainty trickling down to facilities that offer abortion services, like The Lilith Clinic in Portland, Oregon, which has seen an influx of out-of-state patients since last spring.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ALISON EDELMAN (OBGYN OREGON HEALTH AND SCIENCE UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 It's been a huge impact to have our work criminalized basically and not allow us to provide the care for the patient in front of us that we know that's best for them, and they know what's best for them.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For now, women needing abortion services at this particular clinic are expected to wait about one to two weeks. But, medical experts and staff say that could obviously exponentially grow, depending on the future outcome of what happens in Mifepristone's case. Guys.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we know that it's not just the case there. Mireya, thank you so much. Now, let's bring in ABC Supreme Court contributor Kate Shaw. Kate, as we've been reporting, the Supreme Court issued a temporary stay of the Texas judge's order overnight. But tell us, in practical terms, what this means and what happens next.\par \par \uc2 KATE SHAW (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sure thing. So, it's just one week ago that the Texas District Court Judge issued this ruling that, if were allowed to go into effect, would essentially eliminate access to Mifepristone in every state, including states in which abortion is legal and protected. In the interim, a federal appeals court in Texas affirmed in large part what that district court had done, and the opinion essentially blocking Mifepristone was set to go into effect at midnight last night. But just before that deadline, the Supreme Court acting through a single Justice, Justice Alito, issued what is called a temporary administrative stay, which is just a few days of delay to give the Justices a chance to consider the filings of the parties.\par \par \uc2 KATE SHAW (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So for now, that lower court order remains on hold while the Justices consider the filings. And, I should say, it's both the fda and the drug manufacturer asked for this stay, and both of those sets of papers really underscore the stakes. You know, not just access to the most commonly used medication in terminating early pregnancies, Mifepristone, but actually, you know, the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's drug approval process more broadly. This manufacturer says at issue here is federal judges second-guessing the scientific judgment of the experts at the fda. And, if that were allowed to stand it would sew chaos, again as to this drug, but also more broadly.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so it's a win, at least in the short-term, for the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and drug manufacturers, but what is going to be the impact of this latest ruling going forward, and what happens after Wednesday?\par \par \uc2 KATE SHAW (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, short-term Mifepristone remains available everywhere, it is available. And we should say, you know, in states that protect abortion, Mifepristone is commonly prescribed and used, and even in states that have restrictions or even prohibitions on abortion, actually this medication is used in miscarriage management, so it has lawful uses even states that restrict or prohibit abortion.\par \par \uc2 KATE SHAW (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In terms of next steps, the papers will be filed in the next couple of days and the Justices could rule just on the papers that the District Court was incorrect and the Justices could cover restore, in a more permanent way, access to Mifepristone. They could send the case back to the lower courts for another look, or they could schedule a special argument session in May. It would be unusual, but possible for the Justices to do that. But, you know, either way when the Supreme Court overturned Roe Versus Wade last June, it said the Supreme Court is getting out of the business of setting nationwide abortion policy, this is now for the states to decide and we see, I think, the Court is right back sort of in the spotlight. And in some ways, whatever the Court does here, it's going to be having a huge impact on abortion law and policy nationwide.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A huge impact for sure, though uncertain what will happen. Kate Shaw, we appreciate your input this morning. Gio.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4f0005o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINES MISSING CHILDREN RESCUED/SEARCH FOR SAILORS\b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MULROY, LEAK, BLINKEN, TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, HOUSE, BIDEN, PROTESTS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE PROTESTS OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, DOTSON, HEBBE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WRONG HOME FATAL POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 26 MILLION ON ALERT\par \par \uc2 GERSHKOVICH, RUSSIA, ESPIONAGE, MILMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARENTS OF DETAINED JOURNALIST SPEAK OUT\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, KISHIDA, KIMURA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPLOSIVE ATTACK ON JAPAN PM\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, MILITARY COUP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CLASHES IN SUDAN\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, CHILDREN, O'BRIEN, GROSS, MEXICO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSING CHILDREN RESCUED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, 15 missing children were located and multiple arrests were made during a three-day sweep.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities in Pueblo, Colorado, along with \uc2 US Marshals\uc2 , launching the operation focused on finding wanted sex offenders. The children range in age from 15 to 18 years old and were located in several areas in Colorado and California.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR SAILORS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 The US Coast Guard\uc2  and the Mexican navy are searching for three Americans missing at sea.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Frank and Kerry O'Brien, along with William Gross, were last heard from on April 4th as they left Mazatl\u225\'00\'E1n, Mexico. They were on a 44-foot sailboat heading for San Diego. The Coast Guard says that they had planned to stop in Cabo San Lucas, but never showed up.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, remembering the victims a decade after a deadly terrorist attack.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230417ej4f00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WRONG HOME FATAL POLICE SHOOTING 3 OFFICERS ON ADMINISTRATIVE LEAVE AFTER KILLING FATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MULROY, LEAK, BLINKEN, TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, HOUSE, BIDEN, PROTESTS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE PROTESTS OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, DOTSON, HEBBE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WRONG HOME FATAL POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the deadly police-involved shooting in New Mexico, when officers went to the wrong house.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities releasing body camera video. The officers responding to a domestic violence call, but they ended up at the wrong address. Police, opening fire when the man who lived at the house opened the door armed with a handgun.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A warning, that video is disturbing. Here's ABC's Zohreen Shah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 3 OFFICERS ON ADMINISTRATIVE LEAVE AFTER KILLING FATHER\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey.\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Hands up.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, new body camera footage shows the moment police officers in Farmington, New Mexico, shot an innocent man inside his home, just moments after saying they are confused whether they are even at the right address.\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Police (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Police were responding to a late-night domestic violence call on April 5th.\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It is not 5308? That's what it said right there, right?\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 No, it says 5305, isn't it?\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Before the officers could re-assess, 52-year-old Robert Dotson opens his front door and raises his gun.\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey.\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE) (CONTINUED)\par \par \uc2 Hands up.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Police say it's unclear if Dotson fired. Regardless, all three officers shoot at him, killing him. The correct address was right across the street.\par \par \uc2 CHIEF STEVE HEBBE (FARMINGTON POLICE DEPARTMENT)\par \par \uc2 And that's the worst part of this for us is trying to explain that, that we walked right by it to a different address.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also inside the home, Dotson's three children and wife. Cameras pick up her screams.\par \par \uc2 VICTIM'S WIFE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my God. Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Hands up.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She too comes to the doorway also with a gun and pulls the trigger. Police then fire back. Luckily, neither she nor the police are hit.\par \par \uc2 CHIEF STEVE HEBBE (FARMINGTON POLICE DEPARTMENT)\par \par \uc2 She fires out not knowing that it's the police. And I, I absolutely get that. This one, you know, really hurts my heart.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The police chief adds, he is extremely remorseful over the whole thing. Now, the three officers are on administrative leave while the department investigates. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And that investigation just getting started. Zohreen, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230417ej4f00004\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Sour